github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/21742005a40119a8e25c09327c05be5e9f469a41"}],"sha":"2643d5572a93539c5e5a54db0a94ad708e92646e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/2643d5572a93539c5e5a54db0a94ad708e92646e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/21742005a40119a8e25c09327c05be5e9f469a41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:53:40Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:53:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Promote reviewed CB OMOP integration changes onto dev (#1749)\n\n* feat(packaging): make omop_core embeddable as a pip plugin (CB ADR 0001) (#431)\n\nPackage omop_core + omop_oncology + omop_genomics as an installable Django\nplugin (\"promop-omop\") so CancerBot can embed the OMOP-CDM models +\npatient-derivation in-process, WITHOUT patient_portal, the same way CB embeds\nEXACT''s exact_matching. PROMOP itself keeps using these apps in place — no\nrestructure (omop_core structure unchanged, per owner mandate).\n\nTwo surgical portability fixes (models/migration, NOT structure):\n- WearableUpload.uploaded_by: ''patient_portal.Identity'' -> settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL.\n  Reconciles model to migration 0134 (which already targets AUTH_USER_MODEL) —\n  fixes a model<->migration drift; no schema change (in PROMOP both resolve to\n  patient_portal.Identity).\n- omop_core/0071 cross-app dependency on (''patient_portal'',''0002'') made\n  CONDITIONAL on apps.is_installed(''patient_portal''). PROMOP keeps the fresh-\n  install ordering edge; a host without patient_portal (CancerBot) resolves\n  AUTH_USER_MODEL to its own user and the migration graph loads without it.\n  (Django conditional-dependency pattern; codex-validated.)\n\npyproject.toml at repo root packages the three apps via packages.find (apps stay\nin place). Deps: Django>=5.0 + django-oauth-toolkit (omop_core.Organization/0061\nFKs oauth2_provider.Application). Host must also install django.contrib.postgres\n(trigram GIN opclass, migration 0119).\n\nValidated in a CancerBot-like profile (no patient_portal, own auth.User,\noauth2_provider + django.contrib.postgres, pg_trgm+btree_gin):\n- migration graph loads (0071''s patient_portal edge correctly skipped);\n- makemigrations --check -> \"No changes detected\" (no drift, either profile);\n- all 142 omop_core migrations apply into a fresh DB.\n\nNOT packaged: patient_portal-coupled runtime utilities (authorization.py,\norganization_cleanup, signed fhir_export, some management commands) — they stay\nPROMOP-service-only and must not be called from a host lacking patient_portal.\n\nCo-authored-by: Leonid Morozov <lmmobi98@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(matching): in-process ResolvedPatientForMatching adapter (CB ADR 0001, slice 2) (#433)\n\nAdd omop_core.services.patient_matching: an in-process, read-only adapter that\nprojects a persisted PatientRecord into a matcher-consumable patient for the\nembedded exact_matching matcher, so CancerBot can run \"tell, don''t ask\" trial\nmatching on PROMOP-derived patients (EXACT ADR 0004 / CB ADR 0001).\n\n- resolved_patient_for_matching(person): reads the LAST PERSISTED PatientRecord\n  (never calls refresh_patient_record -> no write/derivation on the search read\n  path); returns None if absent (surfaced, not silently derived).\n- MatchingPatient: read-only wrapper satisfying the matcher''s Django-model duck\n  type. Delegates field reads to the record; exposes a class-level _meta FACADE\n  (the matcher reads __class__._meta.get_field for fields lacking a\n  computed_value_type) that returns real PatientRecord fields, and a synthetic\n  CharField for CB-PatientInfo-only computed fields the record has no column for\n  (they read as None -> unknown, interim tri-state). Allows the matcher''s private\n  memo caches (e.g. _pre_existing_condition_codes_cache) without mutating the\n  record; blocks data-field writes. Provides therapy_release_id (a scalar the\n  matcher reads but the record stores only inside therapy_ids_provenance) and a\n  pre_existing_condition_categories related-manager shim (.values_list(\n  ''category__code'')) over the JSON preexisting_conditions column.\n- _therapy_release_id: unanimous-or-null / fail-closed release reducer mirroring\n  PatientRecordSerializer.get_therapy_release_id (EXACT #286 Gate 1). NOTE: a\n  follow-up should extract the serializer''s exact per-line reducer into one shared\n  pure function (incl. its 3L+ handling) instead of this aggregate mirror.\n\nInterim tri-state: no explicit {value,state,authority,provenance} envelope yet;\nabsence stays implicit (no DrugExposure -> NULL/[] columns -> matcher reads as\nunknown, prior_therapy is None not the CB ''None'' asserted-negative). The full\nper-field envelope is a later hardening slice (CB''s ResolvedPatient._raw).\n\nContract/parity test (tests/test_patient_matching.py, importorskip-guarded on\nexact_matching; add the pinned exact-matching via the new [test] extra): the\nmatcher reads all 133 USER_TO_TRIAL_ATTRS_MAPPING attrs off the adapter (get_value\n+ is_attr_blank/_meta.get_field) with zero failures; present-vs-absent, pre-existing\nshape, therapy component/type ids + fail-closed release, interim tri-state, and\nread-only semantics all asserted. 7 pass locally (1 django_db test runs in CI).\n\nCo-authored-by: Leonid Morozov <lmmobi98@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(omop): derive CB-canonical disease from condition_source_value; deterministic condition concept\n\nUnder the CB→PROMOP profile-write path a disease PATCH writes a ConditionOccurrence with the CB canonical\ntitle (e.g. \"multiple myeloma\") in condition_source_value. refresh_patient_record''s _get_disease_data\npreferred the mapped concept_name, which can be a status/subtype variant (\"Multiple myeloma in remission\")\nthat does NOT match EXACT''s trial disease strings. The matcher scopes trials with disease__iexact, so the\nderived variant matched zero trials (and a NULL disease matched cross-disease).\n\n- _get_disease_data: when condition_source_value canonicalizes to a recognized EXACT disease title\n  (_CANONICAL_DISEASES = the lowercase submitted values in CB''s disease_utils / trials.disease), prefer it\n  over concept_name. Non-CB rows (FHIR imports whose source value is a code / free text) are unaffected and\n  keep concept-first behavior.\n- _sync_condition: replace the nondeterministic `concept_name__icontains(...).first()` with a deterministic\n  Condition-domain resolution (exact + standard, then exact, then substring by concept_id), so the stored\n  ConditionOccurrence concept no longer arbitrarily picks a status/subtype variant.\n\nTests (omop_core/tests.py CanonicalizeDiseaseTest, 6 pass): source_value wins over a status-variant concept;\na coded (non-canonical) source value keeps concept-first; _sync_condition resolves the exact concept, not the\nremission variant. Verified live on a 2omop stack: an MM patient''s PatientRecord.disease derives to\n\"multiple myeloma\" and matching scopes to MM trials (Breast Cancer excluded).\n\nTwo-part reviewed (Claude fresh-context: SHIP; codex): codex''s CLL concern refuted — the CB profile UI\nsubmits the lowercase disease value (\"chronic lymphocytic leukemia\"), not the display label, matching the set;\nfresh-context''s domain hardening applied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(cb-merge): honor dev''s lab-alias dedup in retained sync_to_omop; strict xfail\n\nTwo-part review (fresh-context + codex) of the dev→cb back-merge resolutions:\n\n- HIGH (fresh-context): dev''s #471 moved legacy lab aliases (ldh/egfr/creatinine_mg_dl/…)\n  OUT of LAB_FIELD_TO_LOINC into LAB_FIELD_ALIAS_TO_CANONICAL. The cb-retained sync_to_omop\n  gated only on LAB_FIELD_TO_LOINC, so a PATCH to a legacy lab name would silently drop after\n  the merge. Normalize each field through LAB_FIELD_ALIAS_TO_CANONICAL first. (Latent for CB\n  today — CB''s _CB_TO_PROMOP_WRITE writes only canonical names — but correct + future-proof.)\n- MEDIUM (codex): the derive-only contract xfail was strict=False (lingers silently once the\n  module is dropped). strict=True so removing omop_write_service (Phase 4d) forces removing\n  the marker.\n\nConfirmed correct by both reviewers: the #625a graft onto dev''s snapshot-based _get_disease_data\n(cancer_condition/precedence/_usable_concept_name all right); no other file mis-merged. Verified:\ncanonical write path still writes condition + measurement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop_core): descriptor-driven field write applier (apply_field_writes)\n\nPublic single-batch write for the federated PatientInfo editor (CB #2omop-federated-UI\nPhase 2 / A2). Consumes build_writable_field_descriptor and applies it:\n  • KIND_EDITABLE → upsert the OMOP Measurement/Observation the descriptor names\n    (its own concept_id/unit/type/source_value/target), suppressing the per-fact\n    refresh and re-deriving the PatientRecord once at the end.\n  • KIND_PROFILE demographic (gender/race/ethnicity, concept-resolved via\n    demographics.resolve_concept) and location (city/region/postal_code/country/\n    latitude/longitude → the Person''s OMOP Location row, upserted mirroring the\n    persons endpoint) are written directly on the Person.\n  • KIND_PROFILE identity/admin fields (email/phone/validated/…) → result.profile\n    bucket for the caller (this clinical applier does not write them).\n  • everything else (computed/alias/authored/unmapped/unit picker/writable=False) →\n    rejected with the descriptor''s own reason (no silent drop).\n\nFails closed: a null or non-numeric value for a number field raises rather than\nstoring an empty-valued fact. Clears (→ None) are NOT a fact write and are refused\n(safe-delete with provenance is deferred, #4833). Keyed on projection field names, so\nit will replace the CB-interim omop_write_service.sync_to_omop (CB field names) at\nPhase 4d. 9 tests on honest PG: fact write→re-derive round-trip, same-day upsert,\ndemographic write, location upsert+link, replaceable bucketing, computed/unknown\nrejection, null/non-numeric fail-closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop): writable genetic_mutations via list-diff field write\n\nAdd _write_genetic_mutations to apply_field_writes: each mutation is one OMOP\nMeasurement keyed on its gene LOINC (variant->value_as_string,\norigin->qualifier_concept, interpretation->value_as_concept), stamped with a\n''cb-profile:genetic-mutation'' source_value sentinel so the list-diff\nupsert/retire only ever touch rows we authored -- an imported gene fact sharing\nthe 32865 ''Patient self-report'' type is never overwritten or entered-in-error''d.\nGenes dropped from a later PATCH are marked entered-in-error (safe delete); the\nreconcile is scoped by the sentinel, the LOINC vocabulary, and the reviewed gene\ncodes.\n\nFail closed (never silently drop): a non-empty list resolving to no known gene,\na recognized gene without a variant, and a supported-but-unloaded\norigin/interpretation SNOMED concept all raise. owned_writable_fields offers\ngenetic_mutations only when its vocab (type + a gene LOINC) is loaded.\n\n33 tests incl. round-trip, list-diff removal, provenance protection,\nsame-code-other-vocabulary isolation, and the fail-closed paths.\n\nStandalone PROMOP write-path follow-up: healthkey-ai/promop#668\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop): make the 2 direct-boolean assertion social fields writable\n\nThe CB federated editor can now write contraceptive_use and consent_capability (top\ntrial-gating unmapped fields). Map them via their EXISTING LOINC assertion codes\n(8659-8 / 75985-6) with the _get_assertion_data extractor — the SAME concept + reader\nthe projection already uses, so:\n- the federated write round-trips through the existing reader (no second derivation\n  path to clobber it — the flaw an interim CB-DEMO mapping would have had), and\n- the patient''s dated edit is the latest assertion row, so it supersedes an older\n  FHIR-imported assertion of the same concept.\n\n- mappings.DERIVED_FIELD_TO_CODE: +2 entries (contraceptive_use, consent_capability).\n- test_writable_field_descriptor: the attribution invariant now recognizes\n  _get_assertion_data''s data-driven writes (data[field] from _ASSERTION_FIELDS), not\n  only a literal data[''field''].\n- test: True→True / False→False round-trip via apply_field_writes → _get_assertion_data\n  (guards bool(''False'')==True). 154 assertion/descriptor/field-write tests green.\n\nThe 3 inverse_boolean no_* fields (no_mental_health_disorder_status / no_substance_use_status\n/ no_geographic_exposure_risk) need write-side inversion — deferred to healthkey-ai/promop#699.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(episode): let the CB reverse-sync preserve an existing episode_end_date\n\n`upsert_therapy_line_episode`''s update path overwrote `episode_end_date` unconditionally, so passing\n`end_date=None` NULLed a stored date. CB''s profile-write therapy-line path (`_sync_therapy_line`) has no\nend_date field and therefore always passes None — meaning any partial CB therapy edit would erase an\nimported episode''s end date, destroying treatment timing that washout matching relies on.\n\nBut a blanket `end_date is not None` guard would also stop `lot_inference_service._persist_lots` from\nreopening a line it recomputes as ongoing (there None legitimately means \"clear the end date\"). So add\nan explicit `preserve_end_date_when_none` param instead of overloading the value: default False keeps\nthe original None-clears behaviour (lot inference, synthea, FHIR upload); the CB reverse-sync passes\nTrue because its None is always \"omitted\", never \"clear\". start_date already had the equivalent\n`is not None` guard; this makes end_date''s intent explicit rather than symmetric-by-accident.\n\nTests: with the flag, a None end_date preserves the stored date (the CB partial-edit case); without it,\na None end_date still clears (the ongoing-line case).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(omop): resolve therapy-line regimen concept on the CB reverse-sync\n\n_sync_therapy_line reads {prefix}_therapy_concept_id off the write adapter (set\nby CB''s slug->omop_concept_id crosswalk) and stamps it onto the episode object\nAND source concept, so the derivation resolves first_line_therapy_id/name\ninstead of ''Unknown''. A resolved-regimen edit (A->B) must move the source\nconcept too, so upsert_therapy_line_episode gains overwrite_source_concept\n(default off preserves FHIR/enrich asserted concepts; never clears on a null,\nso an unmapped whole-line re-send cannot wipe an imported concept). Warn when a\nresolved id is absent from the package Concept table (vocab skew).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop): write patient staging (stage + TNM) as string Measurements\n\nSlice 2a: sync_to_omop writes the four staging fields (stage 21908-9, tumor\n21905-5, nodes 21906-3, distant_metastasis 21901-4) as patient-authored\nstring-valued Measurements via _sync_string_measurement, so a CB reverse-sync\nstaging edit round-trips: the derivation reads value_as_string and the matcher\ncompares the code verbatim (no normalisation / surface reverse-map needed).\n\nThe upsert key is scoped to the Patient-self-report type (32865) so an imported\nsame-day fact for the same concept is never clobbered, and includes\nmeasurement_source_value so several staging fields that share the generic-concept\nfallback (unloaded LOINC) stay on distinct rows instead of overwriting each other.\n\nAlso drops ''stage'' from the _sync_condition source_value fallback: a staging-only\nedit no longer mints a ConditionOccurrence named after the stage code (which for a\ndisease-less patient created a spurious diagnosis).\n\nReceptor biomarkers (her2/er/pr -> hr/tnbc) are a follow-up (2a-ii): they need\nenum normalisation + a lossy PromopMatchingSurface reverse-map.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(omop): key numeric lab _sync_measurement upsert on measurement_source_value (#4889)\n\nWhen a lab''s LOINC concept is missing from a partially-loaded vocab, _sync_measurement\nfalls back to the generic sentinel (CONCEPT_GENERIC_LAB == 0). The upsert keyed only on\n(person, measurement_concept, measurement_date), so several same-day fields all sharing\nconcept 0 collapsed onto ONE row: the second write overwrote the first field''s value\nwhile keeping the first field''s source, corrupting a neighbour and losing itself. Add\nmeasurement_source_value to the key — for a resolved LOINC concept it is 1:1 with the\nconcept (narrows nothing); for the fallback it keeps each field on its own row. The\ncreate branch already stored source_value=loinc_code, so re-edits still update in place\n(no data migration). The derivation already recovers the field from source_value when\nconcept_code is ''0'', so this aligns the writer with the existing reader.\n\nTests: two same-day generic-fallback labs land on distinct rows (fails pre-fix);\nre-edit updates in place for both resolved and generic-fallback concepts; a same-day\nimported LOINC-coded lab is overwritten in place (pins the pre-existing numeric-path\ntype-scoping gap, tracked in #787).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: model the imported lab with a distinct EHR type so the pin flips under #787 (#4889 review)\n\nCodex review: the imported-fact test used the same type the numeric write stamps, so a future\ntype-scoping fix would not flip it. Give the imported row a distinct EHR type — today the write\nclobbers it in place (key ignores type); when #787 adds type-scoping the write no longer matches\nit, so both assertions must flip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Adapt PROMOP field writes to current descriptors\n\n* Align integration tests with PROMOP descriptor contracts\n\n* Gate genetic mutation editor on loaded vocabularies\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Leonid Morozov <lmmobi98@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8723de745f2b44ddf242689ca309e46603cf3652","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/8723de745f2b44ddf242689ca309e46603cf3652"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/21742005a40119a8e25c09327c05be5e9f469a41","verification":{"payload":"tree 8723de745f2b44ddf242689ca309e46603cf3652\nparent e717ed64f2b7e1f6a57aaac062930ff35b31f4dc\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1791449620 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791449620 +0100\n\nPromote reviewed CB OMOP integration changes onto dev (#1749)\n\n* feat(packaging): make omop_core embeddable as a pip plugin (CB ADR 0001) (#431)\n\nPackage omop_core + omop_oncology + omop_genomics as an installable Django\nplugin (\"promop-omop\") so CancerBot can embed the OMOP-CDM models +\npatient-derivation in-process, WITHOUT patient_portal, the same way CB embeds\nEXACT''s exact_matching. PROMOP itself keeps using these apps in place — no\nrestructure (omop_core structure unchanged, per owner mandate).\n\nTwo surgical portability fixes (models/migration, NOT structure):\n- WearableUpload.uploaded_by: ''patient_portal.Identity'' -> settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL.\n  Reconciles model to migration 0134 (which already targets AUTH_USER_MODEL) —\n  fixes a model<->migration drift; no schema change (in PROMOP both resolve to\n  patient_portal.Identity).\n- omop_core/0071 cross-app dependency on (''patient_portal'',''0002'') made\n  CONDITIONAL on apps.is_installed(''patient_portal''). PROMOP keeps the fresh-\n  install ordering edge; a host without patient_portal (CancerBot) resolves\n  AUTH_USER_MODEL to its own user and the migration graph loads without it.\n  (Django conditional-dependency pattern; codex-validated.)\n\npyproject.toml at repo root packages the three apps via packages.find (apps stay\nin place). Deps: Django>=5.0 + django-oauth-toolkit (omop_core.Organization/0061\nFKs oauth2_provider.Application). Host must also install django.contrib.postgres\n(trigram GIN opclass, migration 0119).\n\nValidated in a CancerBot-like profile (no patient_portal, own auth.User,\noauth2_provider + django.contrib.postgres, pg_trgm+btree_gin):\n- migration graph loads (0071''s patient_portal edge correctly skipped);\n- makemigrations --check -> \"No changes detected\" (no drift, either profile);\n- all 142 omop_core migrations apply into a fresh DB.\n\nNOT packaged: patient_portal-coupled runtime utilities (authorization.py,\norganization_cleanup, signed fhir_export, some management commands) — they stay\nPROMOP-service-only and must not be called from a host lacking patient_portal.\n\nCo-authored-by: Leonid Morozov <lmmobi98@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(matching): in-process ResolvedPatientForMatching adapter (CB ADR 0001, slice 2) (#433)\n\nAdd omop_core.services.patient_matching: an in-process, read-only adapter that\nprojects a persisted PatientRecord into a matcher-consumable patient for the\nembedded exact_matching matcher, so CancerBot can run \"tell, don''t ask\" trial\nmatching on PROMOP-derived patients (EXACT ADR 0004 / CB ADR 0001).\n\n- resolved_patient_for_matching(person): reads the LAST PERSISTED PatientRecord\n  (never calls refresh_patient_record -> no write/derivation on the search read\n  path); returns None if absent (surfaced, not silently derived).\n- MatchingPatient: read-only wrapper satisfying the matcher''s Django-model duck\n  type. Delegates field reads to the record; exposes a class-level _meta FACADE\n  (the matcher reads __class__._meta.get_field for fields lacking a\n  computed_value_type) that returns real PatientRecord fields, and a synthetic\n  CharField for CB-PatientInfo-only computed fields the record has no column for\n  (they read as None -> unknown, interim tri-state). Allows the matcher''s private\n  memo caches (e.g. _pre_existing_condition_codes_cache) without mutating the\n  record; blocks data-field writes. Provides therapy_release_id (a scalar the\n  matcher reads but the record stores only inside therapy_ids_provenance) and a\n  pre_existing_condition_categories related-manager shim (.values_list(\n  ''category__code'')) over the JSON preexisting_conditions column.\n- _therapy_release_id: unanimous-or-null / fail-closed release reducer mirroring\n  PatientRecordSerializer.get_therapy_release_id (EXACT #286 Gate 1). NOTE: a\n  follow-up should extract the serializer''s exact per-line reducer into one shared\n  pure function (incl. its 3L+ handling) instead of this aggregate mirror.\n\nInterim tri-state: no explicit {value,state,authority,provenance} envelope yet;\nabsence stays implicit (no DrugExposure -> NULL/[] columns -> matcher reads as\nunknown, prior_therapy is None not the CB ''None'' asserted-negative). The full\nper-field envelope is a later hardening slice (CB''s ResolvedPatient._raw).\n\nContract/parity test (tests/test_patient_matching.py, importorskip-guarded on\nexact_matching; add the pinned exact-matching via the new [test] extra): the\nmatcher reads all 133 USER_TO_TRIAL_ATTRS_MAPPING attrs off the adapter (get_value\n+ is_attr_blank/_meta.get_field) with zero failures; present-vs-absent, pre-existing\nshape, therapy component/type ids + fail-closed release, interim tri-state, and\nread-only semantics all asserted. 7 pass locally (1 django_db test runs in CI).\n\nCo-authored-by: Leonid Morozov <lmmobi98@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(omop): derive CB-canonical disease from condition_source_value; deterministic condition concept\n\nUnder the CB→PROMOP profile-write path a disease PATCH writes a ConditionOccurrence with the CB canonical\ntitle (e.g. \"multiple myeloma\") in condition_source_value. refresh_patient_record''s _get_disease_data\npreferred the mapped concept_name, which can be a status/subtype variant (\"Multiple myeloma in remission\")\nthat does NOT match EXACT''s trial disease strings. The matcher scopes trials with disease__iexact, so the\nderived variant matched zero trials (and a NULL disease matched cross-disease).\n\n- _get_disease_data: when condition_source_value canonicalizes to a recognized EXACT disease title\n  (_CANONICAL_DISEASES = the lowercase submitted values in CB''s disease_utils / trials.disease), prefer it\n  over concept_name. Non-CB rows (FHIR imports whose source value is a code / free text) are unaffected and\n  keep concept-first behavior.\n- _sync_condition: replace the nondeterministic `concept_name__icontains(...).first()` with a deterministic\n  Condition-domain resolution (exact + standard, then exact, then substring by concept_id), so the stored\n  ConditionOccurrence concept no longer arbitrarily picks a status/subtype variant.\n\nTests (omop_core/tests.py CanonicalizeDiseaseTest, 6 pass): source_value wins over a status-variant concept;\na coded (non-canonical) source value keeps concept-first; _sync_condition resolves the exact concept, not the\nremission variant. Verified live on a 2omop stack: an MM patient''s PatientRecord.disease derives to\n\"multiple myeloma\" and matching scopes to MM trials (Breast Cancer excluded).\n\nTwo-part reviewed (Claude fresh-context: SHIP; codex): codex''s CLL concern refuted — the CB profile UI\nsubmits the lowercase disease value (\"chronic lymphocytic leukemia\"), not the display label, matching the set;\nfresh-context''s domain hardening applied.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(cb-merge): honor dev''s lab-alias dedup in retained sync_to_omop; strict xfail\n\nTwo-part review (fresh-context + codex) of the dev→cb back-merge resolutions:\n\n- HIGH (fresh-context): dev''s #471 moved legacy lab aliases (ldh/egfr/creatinine_mg_dl/…)\n  OUT of LAB_FIELD_TO_LOINC into LAB_FIELD_ALIAS_TO_CANONICAL. The cb-retained sync_to_omop\n  gated only on LAB_FIELD_TO_LOINC, so a PATCH to a legacy lab name would silently drop after\n  the merge. Normalize each field through LAB_FIELD_ALIAS_TO_CANONICAL first. (Latent for CB\n  today — CB''s _CB_TO_PROMOP_WRITE writes only canonical names — but correct + future-proof.)\n- MEDIUM (codex): the derive-only contract xfail was strict=False (lingers silently once the\n  module is dropped). strict=True so removing omop_write_service (Phase 4d) forces removing\n  the marker.\n\nConfirmed correct by both reviewers: the #625a graft onto dev''s snapshot-based _get_disease_data\n(cancer_condition/precedence/_usable_concept_name all right); no other file mis-merged. Verified:\ncanonical write path still writes condition + measurement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop_core): descriptor-driven field write applier (apply_field_writes)\n\nPublic single-batch write for the federated PatientInfo editor (CB #2omop-federated-UI\nPhase 2 / A2). Consumes build_writable_field_descriptor and applies it:\n  • KIND_EDITABLE → upsert the OMOP Measurement/Observation the descriptor names\n    (its own concept_id/unit/type/source_value/target), suppressing the per-fact\n    refresh and re-deriving the PatientRecord once at the end.\n  • KIND_PROFILE demographic (gender/race/ethnicity, concept-resolved via\n    demographics.resolve_concept) and location (city/region/postal_code/country/\n    latitude/longitude → the Person''s OMOP Location row, upserted mirroring the\n    persons endpoint) are written directly on the Person.\n  • KIND_PROFILE identity/admin fields (email/phone/validated/…) → result.profile\n    bucket for the caller (this clinical applier does not write them).\n  • everything else (computed/alias/authored/unmapped/unit picker/writable=False) →\n    rejected with the descriptor''s own reason (no silent drop).\n\nFails closed: a null or non-numeric value for a number field raises rather than\nstoring an empty-valued fact. Clears (→ None) are NOT a fact write and are refused\n(safe-delete with provenance is deferred, #4833). Keyed on projection field names, so\nit will replace the CB-interim omop_write_service.sync_to_omop (CB field names) at\nPhase 4d. 9 tests on honest PG: fact write→re-derive round-trip, same-day upsert,\ndemographic write, location upsert+link, replaceable bucketing, computed/unknown\nrejection, null/non-numeric fail-closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop): writable genetic_mutations via list-diff field write\n\nAdd _write_genetic_mutations to apply_field_writes: each mutation is one OMOP\nMeasurement keyed on its gene LOINC (variant->value_as_string,\norigin->qualifier_concept, interpretation->value_as_concept), stamped with a\n''cb-profile:genetic-mutation'' source_value sentinel so the list-diff\nupsert/retire only ever touch rows we authored -- an imported gene fact sharing\nthe 32865 ''Patient self-report'' type is never overwritten or entered-in-error''d.\nGenes dropped from a later PATCH are marked entered-in-error (safe delete); the\nreconcile is scoped by the sentinel, the LOINC vocabulary, and the reviewed gene\ncodes.\n\nFail closed (never silently drop): a non-empty list resolving to no known gene,\na recognized gene without a variant, and a supported-but-unloaded\norigin/interpretation SNOMED concept all raise. owned_writable_fields offers\ngenetic_mutations only when its vocab (type + a gene LOINC) is loaded.\n\n33 tests incl. round-trip, list-diff removal, provenance protection,\nsame-code-other-vocabulary isolation, and the fail-closed paths.\n\nStandalone PROMOP write-path follow-up: healthkey-ai/promop#668\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop): make the 2 direct-boolean assertion social fields writable\n\nThe CB federated editor can now write contraceptive_use and consent_capability (top\ntrial-gating unmapped fields). Map them via their EXISTING LOINC assertion codes\n(8659-8 / 75985-6) with the _get_assertion_data extractor — the SAME concept + reader\nthe projection already uses, so:\n- the federated write round-trips through the existing reader (no second derivation\n  path to clobber it — the flaw an interim CB-DEMO mapping would have had), and\n- the patient''s dated edit is the latest assertion row, so it supersedes an older\n  FHIR-imported assertion of the same concept.\n\n- mappings.DERIVED_FIELD_TO_CODE: +2 entries (contraceptive_use, consent_capability).\n- test_writable_field_descriptor: the attribution invariant now recognizes\n  _get_assertion_data''s data-driven writes (data[field] from _ASSERTION_FIELDS), not\n  only a literal data[''field''].\n- test: True→True / False→False round-trip via apply_field_writes → _get_assertion_data\n  (guards bool(''False'')==True). 154 assertion/descriptor/field-write tests green.\n\nThe 3 inverse_boolean no_* fields (no_mental_health_disorder_status / no_substance_use_status\n/ no_geographic_exposure_risk) need write-side inversion — deferred to healthkey-ai/promop#699.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(episode): let the CB reverse-sync preserve an existing episode_end_date\n\n`upsert_therapy_line_episode`''s update path overwrote `episode_end_date` unconditionally, so passing\n`end_date=None` NULLed a stored date. CB''s profile-write therapy-line path (`_sync_therapy_line`) has no\nend_date field and therefore always passes None — meaning any partial CB therapy edit would erase an\nimported episode''s end date, destroying treatment timing that washout matching relies on.\n\nBut a blanket `end_date is not None` guard would also stop `lot_inference_service._persist_lots` from\nreopening a line it recomputes as ongoing (there None legitimately means \"clear the end date\"). So add\nan explicit `preserve_end_date_when_none` param instead of overloading the value: default False keeps\nthe original None-clears behaviour (lot inference, synthea, FHIR upload); the CB reverse-sync passes\nTrue because its None is always \"omitted\", never \"clear\". start_date already had the equivalent\n`is not None` guard; this makes end_date''s intent explicit rather than symmetric-by-accident.\n\nTests: with the flag, a None end_date preserves the stored date (the CB partial-edit case); without it,\na None end_date still clears (the ongoing-line case).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(omop): resolve therapy-line regimen concept on the CB reverse-sync\n\n_sync_therapy_line reads {prefix}_therapy_concept_id off the write adapter (set\nby CB''s slug->omop_concept_id crosswalk) and stamps it onto the episode object\nAND source concept, so the derivation resolves first_line_therapy_id/name\ninstead of ''Unknown''. A resolved-regimen edit (A->B) must move the source\nconcept too, so upsert_therapy_line_episode gains overwrite_source_concept\n(default off preserves FHIR/enrich asserted concepts; never clears on a null,\nso an unmapped whole-line re-send cannot wipe an imported concept). Warn when a\nresolved id is absent from the package Concept table (vocab skew).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(omop): write patient staging (stage + TNM) as string Measurements\n\nSlice 2a: sync_to_omop writes the four staging fields (stage 21908-9, tumor\n21905-5, nodes 21906-3, distant_metastasis 21901-4) as patient-authored\nstring-valued Measurements via _sync_string_measurement, so a CB reverse-sync\nstaging edit round-trips: the derivation reads value_as_string and the matcher\ncompares the code verbatim (no normalisation / surface reverse-map needed).\n\nThe upsert key is scoped to the Patient-self-report type (32865) so an imported\nsame-day fact for the same concept is never clobbered, and includes\nmeasurement_source_value so several staging fields that share the generic-concept\nfallback (unloaded LOINC) stay on distinct rows instead of overwriting each other.\n\nAlso drops ''stage'' from the _sync_condition source_value fallback: a staging-only\nedit no longer mints a ConditionOccurrence named after the stage code (which for a\ndisease-less patient created a spurious diagnosis).\n\nReceptor biomarkers (her2/er/pr -> hr/tnbc) are a follow-up (2a-ii): they need\nenum normalisation + a lossy PromopMatchingSurface reverse-map.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(omop): key numeric lab _sync_measurement upsert on measurement_source_value (#4889)\n\nWhen a lab''s LOINC concept is missing from a partially-loaded vocab, _sync_measurement\nfalls back to the generic sentinel (CONCEPT_GENERIC_LAB == 0). The upsert keyed only on\n(person, measurement_concept, measurement_date), so several same-day fields all sharing\nconcept 0 collapsed onto ONE row: the second write overwrote the first field''s value\nwhile keeping the first field''s source, corrupting a neighbour and losing itself. Add\nmeasurement_source_value to the key — for a resolved LOINC concept it is 1:1 with the\nconcept (narrows nothing); for the fallback it keeps each field on its own row. The\ncreate branch already stored source_value=loinc_code, so re-edits still update in place\n(no data migration). The derivation already recovers the field from source_value when\nconcept_code is ''0'', so this aligns the writer with the existing reader.\n\nTests: two same-day generic-fallback labs land on distinct rows (fails pre-fix);\nre-edit updates in place for both resolved and generic-fallback concepts; a same-day\nimported LOINC-coded lab is overwritten in place (pins the pre-existing numeric-path\ntype-scoping gap, tracked in #787).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: model the imported lab with a distinct EHR type so the pin flips under #787 (#4889 review)\n\nCodex review: the imported-fact test used the same type the numeric write stamps, so a future\ntype-scoping fix would not flip it. Give the imported row a distinct EHR type — today the write\nclobbers it in place (key ignores type); when #787 adds type-scoping the write no longer matches\nit, so both assertions must flip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Adapt PROMOP field writes to current descriptors\n\n* Align integration tests with PROMOP descriptor contracts\n\n* Gate genetic mutation editor on loaded vocabularies\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Leonid Morozov <lmmobi98@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1oUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo0kQAJs9GICwVXjZSLImg+10npfE\ngh2qICqRwgwlF6wkTLSeNNHcV+WXcL5mQvN3NXJAb7ZMnB3EDqIcj1OqZkh0euc0\nRarywLBOKz5zhPnB4uiiljBUW6AeOzsTLcLvaZZI5KEAGKpyWZlu3m7ufpHZpD1A\nHck30kNdhV2C2aD0+DOmu3GO596FlS5K+2hLfdlJhivi8FSEhDJ8jZrvJVpTxKhr\npQEcqMpXtkiAwKHrnHScNTKXhwoQsjvTkuQRFF+83ZrUgKiEXYvRMwmWeIGpKzqd\nUDaO01i589s/FGC0gVgvyIsVuT4NKN2ZQbxci0NefeV5EenAXjBOTLsC52JCw/61\ndbYJiiRsA6E3zdJMCNqqy1nlJqTED8uX3MUWCHgKM1U1ud49QFPkfIDQwSu8joqg\nS/G8EdxkAVGI/sWmeevzKNFyOTKqs52tymDRy0uUrrlabtSors8/UGCYnvTk4j+1\ntr8wowOl04i11A8e7niz8qZ0SSBAfTmddknWRICf/4tQIdJpfqvM0Ht6HY38Y2N8\nmLVJpAG/SS8gHRG+bjsDY6/KfuJ/Dx7XfvfxSRG5KCbDhJ20hZQTOjTjXx+rf+qP\noavMqQ3naMdD0WV9vXmQJRQYB6ld/U2AdC8dbcebn1J3F+Y+gwAq7xIFnXIARY76\nhGYd1OFJWON2vfUwOUec\n=+2G2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:53:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/21742005a40119a8e25c09327c05be5e9f469a41","node_id":"C_kwDOPw6uhdoAKDIxNzQyMDA1YTQwMTE5YThlMjVjMDkzMjdjMDViZTVlOWY0NjlhNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/e717ed64f2b7e1f6a57aaac062930ff35b31f4dc","sha":"e717ed64f2b7e1f6a57aaac062930ff35b31f4dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/e717ed64f2b7e1f6a57aaac062930ff35b31f4dc"}],"sha":"21742005a40119a8e25c09327c05be5e9f469a41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/21742005a40119a8e25c09327c05be5e9f469a41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/e717ed64f2b7e1f6a57aaac062930ff35b31f4dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:43:47Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:43:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(imaging): structured imaging studies from FHIR (#1731) (#1750)\n\n* feat(imaging): structured imaging studies from FHIR (#1731)\n\nRadiology DiagnosticReports and ImagingStudy resources are imported as\nstructured studies, recorded in ADR 0003:\n\n- the study is a procedure_occurrence at the performing facility''s visit;\n- a new image_occurrence table (OHDSI Medical Imaging CDM) holds the\n  modality, body site, DICOM study UID and the source''s image link;\n- the radiologist''s impression is a note kept byte-for-byte, the rest of\n  the report another note, linked through the OMOP 5.4 note_event_id\n  columns added to note; findings are note_nlp rows;\n- contrast is an observation linked to the procedure;\n- the report file is a PatientDocument linked by procedure_occurrence_id.\n\nBoth FHIR import paths (upload and provider sync) call one service;\nre-importing a study rewrites it in place. imaging_studies(person) reads\nthe studies back for the PHR. Migration 0282 adds the table, the columns\nand the image_occurrence and note_nlp PK sequences.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(imaging): read contrast from the study code''s displays too\n\nA report''s code text is often a friendly name (\"Prostate MRI,\nmultiparametric\") while its codings say \"MR Prostate WO and W contrast IV\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(imaging): classify image_occurrence as patient data\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(imaging): carry imaging studies through patient transfer\n\nCopying a patient copies image_occurrence and re-links the report notes\n(note_event_id, through its field concept) and a report document''s\nprocedure_occurrence_id to the copied study.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(imaging): harden the FHIR imaging import (#1731 review)\n\nReview findings on the untrusted-input side of the importer:\n\n- The contrast pattern and the HTML tag strip are linear on hostile text\n  (bounded gaps, ''<[^<>]*>'', each text capped at 1,000 characters); 80 KB of\n  crafted text took 12.8 s before.\n- In a multi-patient upload a report only reaches its own patient''s\n  ImagingStudy and finding Observations; the bundle index is built once.\n- Only a performing Organization is a facility: a Practitioner performer no\n  longer crashes the import or becomes a care site.\n- A study is found again by its identity (new local column\n  image_source_value: DICOM UID, else report or study id), so two studies with\n  the same code on the same day stay two; adoption only takes a plain EHR\n  procedure row (never another study, never a patient-entered one) and only\n  upgrades its concept from 0.\n- entered-in-error / cancelled reports are skipped and retract an earlier\n  import of the same study.\n\nADR 0003 updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(imaging): renumber the imaging migration after dev''s 0282 (#1731)\n\ndev gained omop_core/0282_patient_source_code (#1745), so the PR''s merge\nwith dev had two 0282 leaves and CI''s Django runner stopped with\n\"Conflicting migrations detected\". Merge dev and make the imaging migration\n0283, depending on 0282_patient_source_code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c654b1da3f8f7caad9eeb7abfe286ede811b8b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/c654b1da3f8f7caad9eeb7abfe286ede811b8b20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/e717ed64f2b7e1f6a57aaac062930ff35b31f4dc","verification":{"payload":"tree c654b1da3f8f7caad9eeb7abfe286ede811b8b20\nparent 28da5c057020b64889b00053a58a0670635da3d6\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1791449027 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791449027 +0100\n\nfeat(imaging): structured imaging studies from FHIR (#1731) (#1750)\n\n* feat(imaging): structured imaging studies from FHIR (#1731)\n\nRadiology DiagnosticReports and ImagingStudy resources are imported as\nstructured studies, recorded in ADR 0003:\n\n- the study is a procedure_occurrence at the performing facility''s visit;\n- a new image_occurrence table (OHDSI Medical Imaging CDM) holds the\n  modality, body site, DICOM study UID and the source''s image link;\n- the radiologist''s impression is a note kept byte-for-byte, the rest of\n  the report another note, linked through the OMOP 5.4 note_event_id\n  columns added to note; findings are note_nlp rows;\n- contrast is an observation linked to the procedure;\n- the report file is a PatientDocument linked by procedure_occurrence_id.\n\nBoth FHIR import paths (upload and provider sync) call one service;\nre-importing a study rewrites it in place. imaging_studies(person) reads\nthe studies back for the PHR. Migration 0282 adds the table, the columns\nand the image_occurrence and note_nlp PK sequences.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(imaging): read contrast from the study code''s displays too\n\nA report''s code text is often a friendly name (\"Prostate MRI,\nmultiparametric\") while its codings say \"MR Prostate WO and W contrast IV\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(imaging): classify image_occurrence as patient data\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(imaging): carry imaging studies through patient transfer\n\nCopying a patient copies image_occurrence and re-links the report notes\n(note_event_id, through its field concept) and a report document''s\nprocedure_occurrence_id to the copied study.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(imaging): harden the FHIR imaging import (#1731 review)\n\nReview findings on the untrusted-input side of the importer:\n\n- The contrast pattern and the HTML tag strip are linear on hostile text\n  (bounded gaps, ''<[^<>]*>'', each text capped at 1,000 characters); 80 KB of\n  crafted text took 12.8 s before.\n- In a multi-patient upload a report only reaches its own patient''s\n  ImagingStudy and finding Observations; the bundle index is built once.\n- Only a performing Organization is a facility: a Practitioner performer no\n  longer crashes the import or becomes a care site.\n- A study is found again by its identity (new local column\n  image_source_value: DICOM UID, else report or study id), so two studies with\n  the same code on the same day stay two; adoption only takes a plain EHR\n  procedure row (never another study, never a patient-entered one) and only\n  upgrades its concept from 0.\n- entered-in-error / cancelled reports are skipped and retract an earlier\n  import of the same study.\n\nADR 0003 updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(imaging): renumber the imaging migration after dev''s 0282 (#1731)\n\ndev gained omop_core/0282_patient_source_code (#1745), so the PR''s merge\nwith dev had two 0282 leaves and CI''s Django runner stopped with\n\"Conflicting migrations detected\". Merge dev and make the imaging migration\n0283, depending on 0282_patient_source_code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1fDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAASIQABiN78MZfpCxOzN7TwI3Jwyx\nlpD/EsfUBPAA5k75Bid7huq/E+6Tzo4/KXq0eHRr/WvVOiJ9HmtxvNz+mz4c88zj\nDcGeD7P8xqlOQIM8N3be2JiBYn5Hjk00s74RNhHPVl/kAaEMKtjfdt7ZhZLB4lYI\neWNeK9CeMhTw8eeH0iJHE0dmMMTnicJLJYQIGvm3XO8rYySW1S861V+4HlMwhZS0\nLL4PD5Pe3l1JguVFP0JfxQxcA/13Y6N6GmaoAs3SuTkhPMovOiL55mKVu2mn5+1Y\nvP+c5oGkvNGAksZl8WEQ4VReBI81PQbe+Ay83T072TCahryQcP2Hb0YDfhKdhNJK\nt6XZZiTHQntKdrZwXRwT5aV8XEOFqPHTq7dnikB4qQ6ER51M/fkP655Ioaj2O/x9\nFnZ34+GAHQE2T/5f96fuwVhkwN/Gt9TSQNVBEMJ/3mZLXqcaOdgjulsqwX5knuBx\ngEIzrwYVqXUNXqgyEP4k7IdofBq6/R3TFShmwerzWZGDuJ16HHSczTPLuW0Dp6co\nu45OU7Sh2uARwej8nAxauYPRVvINPwrPSVfrVDWgKmauyaOunf6++vNShWzTsf0G\n0nQEFDNYMaXmy7lhgTDbPXbfGwfDbx/u67DAEAncnI9GcX+xlak95VrU+MhVpAKB\nx+jZmM/OwiNxez+WWdIA\n=PnPz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:43:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.