https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/18d1af216ee7c5c1971c5aff4a8315fd14b28238/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:22:57Z","email":"adam@healthkey.ai","name":"Adam Blum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:22:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Source Codes tab and Generate OMOP for patient records (#1742)\n\n* WIP: Patient source codes — Issues 1-2 backend + plan\n\nAdd plan doc and initial implementation:\n- GET /api/v1/patient-records/{person_id}/source-codes/ (Issue 1)\n- POST /api/v1/patient-records/{person_id}/resolve-source-codes/ (Issue 2)\n- resolve_person_source_codes() in code_resolution.py\n- _aggregate_patient_source_codes() helper in views.py\n\nIssues 3-5 (bulk resolve, frontend) still pending.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Source Codes tab and Generate OMOP for patient records\n\nIssues 1-5: Add patient source codes endpoint, per-patient and bulk\nresolve-source-codes endpoints, Source Codes tab on patient detail,\nand bulk Generate OMOP action on patient list.\n\nBackend:\n- GET /v1/patient-records/{id}/source-codes/ aggregates distinct\n  source codes across all clinical tables with mapping status\n- POST /v1/patient-records/{id}/resolve-source-codes/ re-resolves\n  unmapped/quarantine rows using approved SCCM mappings\n- POST /v1/patient-records/bulk_resolve_source_codes/ dispatches\n  bulk resolution via Celery/inline with poll endpoint\n- SourceCodeResolveRun model tracks bulk run progress\n- 14 backend tests covering aggregation, resolution, bulk, and auth\n\nFrontend:\n- PatientSourceCodesTab component with summary, filters, Generate\n  OMOP button, and source codes table\n- Source Codes tab added to PatientDetail admin tabs\n- Generate OMOP bulk action on PatientList with progress dialog\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address code review findings for patient source codes\n\n- Fix critical URL mismatch: frontend used underscores for\n  bulk-resolve-source-codes but backend uses hyphens (would 404)\n- Fix N+1 SCCM queries: batch-fetch mappings per table instead of\n  one query per source value\n- Fix vocabulary_id bug: query SCCM directly instead of going through\n  approved_mapping_for('''') which misses rows with real vocabulary IDs\n- Fix polling interval leak: store in ref, clean up on unmount\n- Fix crash resilience: wrap bulk resolve loop in try/except, set\n  state=FAILED on crash instead of leaving RUNNING forever\n- Fix person_ids storage: pass through task args instead of repurposing\n  error_detail JSONField\n- Add person_ids element-type validation (must be integers)\n- Group aggregation by source_value only (not source_value + concept_id)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Adam Blum <23161+adamblum@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a504631bc8928fc19d9020703ef5acd90388b60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/4a504631bc8928fc19d9020703ef5acd90388b60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/18d1af216ee7c5c1971c5aff4a8315fd14b28238","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a504631bc8928fc19d9020703ef5acd90388b60\nparent 034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746\nauthor Adam Blum <adam@healthkey.ai> 1791375777 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791375777 +0100\n\nfeat: Source Codes tab and Generate OMOP for patient records (#1742)\n\n* WIP: Patient source codes — Issues 1-2 backend + plan\n\nAdd plan doc and initial implementation:\n- GET /api/v1/patient-records/{person_id}/source-codes/ (Issue 1)\n- POST /api/v1/patient-records/{person_id}/resolve-source-codes/ (Issue 2)\n- resolve_person_source_codes() in code_resolution.py\n- _aggregate_patient_source_codes() helper in views.py\n\nIssues 3-5 (bulk resolve, frontend) still pending.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Source Codes tab and Generate OMOP for patient records\n\nIssues 1-5: Add patient source codes endpoint, per-patient and bulk\nresolve-source-codes endpoints, Source Codes tab on patient detail,\nand bulk Generate OMOP action on patient list.\n\nBackend:\n- GET /v1/patient-records/{id}/source-codes/ aggregates distinct\n  source codes across all clinical tables with mapping status\n- POST /v1/patient-records/{id}/resolve-source-codes/ re-resolves\n  unmapped/quarantine rows using approved SCCM mappings\n- POST /v1/patient-records/bulk_resolve_source_codes/ dispatches\n  bulk resolution via Celery/inline with poll endpoint\n- SourceCodeResolveRun model tracks bulk run progress\n- 14 backend tests covering aggregation, resolution, bulk, and auth\n\nFrontend:\n- PatientSourceCodesTab component with summary, filters, Generate\n  OMOP button, and source codes table\n- Source Codes tab added to PatientDetail admin tabs\n- Generate OMOP bulk action on PatientList with progress dialog\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address code review findings for patient source codes\n\n- Fix critical URL mismatch: frontend used underscores for\n  bulk-resolve-source-codes but backend uses hyphens (would 404)\n- Fix N+1 SCCM queries: batch-fetch mappings per table instead of\n  one query per source value\n- Fix vocabulary_id bug: query SCCM directly instead of going through\n  approved_mapping_for('''') which misses rows with real vocabulary IDs\n- Fix polling interval leak: store in ref, clean up on unmount\n- Fix crash resilience: wrap bulk resolve loop in try/except, set\n  state=FAILED on crash instead of leaving RUNNING forever\n- Fix person_ids storage: pass through task args instead of repurposing\n  error_detail JSONField\n- Add person_ids element-type validation (must be integers)\n- Group aggregation by source_value only (not source_value + concept_id)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Adam Blum <23161+adamblum@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxjmhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6okQAKncFF3ZFgDJYuNSe+/+gjPN\nqH2+hjbFLa5e65lIVxYiVsjRjKKGS2R1XDbrPF8EcWecg/XzRaV3NLTyjtRstm7D\n89+8gRPVfJLFAvTgLrBom7Q4Cn+QfRuUrgInNRdKiyq2tkTSWw5gMlwhni9hn+Ym\nFthruJXBPyxd1dWdDsuwzFvxm76SiGeSwCqOU7313UxpR9RasP13pmqCj23QQYfl\n+h5SV5L/n845aCD/UQzsXX5b1ETiQgDu34FBDNwo4/qWBiErxNDYF5hiUYG8boqU\nrYiXGnOy69+OlobKJxUXfuqcDWrIW7FKTSTdRs0eMcUCkZ0Isa++eVlBUJm9kLNl\n3htuiV7ZXbsrklyBWBowM2uuwRZ8MHgtEA9rKDKeuDDwDJS1zrYrDBqWXDW1JhUq\nfYpjFJ6q+kH3Ch86FXUKWWpM8JUm+3NoJUdutYr2IBKEW+dlLXCAtdwDt+U89xN2\n+hpj3o7yobqlcJY6HixmPPIrMVfbcHZpw1sekEcqygdN1/3Ddwlh7XfSzuUyI/wL\nPlGIbmUvh6aadPOT4v7kES5TJjo0rZxMr7orod0inAtMk8DYRluJmqLpd86DrALu\nxINBiuecerRPFZ17PeNTtQmCc5ZBxhOsgEuKByuWysR+K9stDrdxd6W9SRr+93Jd\nEoJJsAyKBxNAuLHuUoYL\n=ww8X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T12:22:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/18d1af216ee7c5c1971c5aff4a8315fd14b28238","node_id":"C_kwDOPw6uhdoAKDE4ZDFhZjIxNmVlN2M1YzE5NzFjNWFmZjRhODMxNWZkMTRiMjgyMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746","sha":"034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746"}],"sha":"18d1af216ee7c5c1971c5aff4a8315fd14b28238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/18d1af216ee7c5c1971c5aff4a8315fd14b28238"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:06:19Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:06:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(patient): advance directive upload never sent the document (#1730)\n\nUploading an advance directive always failed with \"Failed to upload advance\ndirective.\" The file never reached the server.\n\nThe shared api instance declares ''Content-Type: application/json'' as a\ndefault, and axios reads that header when it decides how to encode the body.\nFor FormData it takes the JSON branch -- it stringifies the entries, and every\nFile collapses to {}. The documents viewset''s FileField then saw no upload, the\nrow was rejected, and the catch turned the reason into one generic line. Same\nmechanism as #1729, which fixed the Code Mapping dialog.\n\nClearing the header for this request lets the browser set multipart/form-data\nwith its own boundary, which is what the endpoint has always expected.\n\nThere was no test on this component, so the fix is covered by a new one that\nasserts the body stays FormData with the File intact and the per-request header\nis cleared; removing the fix fails it. A second case pins the error path.\n\nThe pre-existing exhaustive-deps warning on the fetch callback is untouched\nand unrelated.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4447bf9abad2a9745c0c67d06ba5bc9857867618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/4447bf9abad2a9745c0c67d06ba5bc9857867618"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746","verification":{"payload":"tree 4447bf9abad2a9745c0c67d06ba5bc9857867618\nparent d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1791219979 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791219979 +0300\n\nfix(patient): advance directive upload never sent the document (#1730)\n\nUploading an advance directive always failed with \"Failed to upload advance\ndirective.\" The file never reached the server.\n\nThe shared api instance declares ''Content-Type: application/json'' as a\ndefault, and axios reads that header when it decides how to encode the body.\nFor FormData it takes the JSON branch -- it stringifies the entries, and every\nFile collapses to {}. The documents viewset''s FileField then saw no upload, the\nrow was rejected, and the catch turned the reason into one generic line. Same\nmechanism as #1729, which fixed the Code Mapping dialog.\n\nClearing the header for this request lets the browser set multipart/form-data\nwith its own boundary, which is what the endpoint has always expected.\n\nThere was no test on this component, so the fix is covered by a new one that\nasserts the body stays FormData with the File intact and the per-request header\nis cleared; removing the fix fails it. A second case pins the error path.\n\nThe pre-existing exhaustive-deps warning on the fetch callback is untouched\nand unrelated.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw9kLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQEEQACqbz9dQZQWGSTEag6SRAl6H\niDYdpdEwcHTz5vfxM63HbnJV4JG4nAydBa6e7zbSedLCqmDxx9UcXA1Y2lJY+zeG\nRI1ljBdpvIXz7y7/0PFy1IUc/c+vKkrjSVigjBvBpd8T06nf6LKTvkIo20DYik+n\n5G6zL3YZfeu2M0vedHXGKiWUbltw1cZ5Zockcz532Mg8TZ8nuRoZRDX9Oxm9af5t\n3VkFeShcRyyPTeRRRJbA9a4/2PmeOP7yvIrLO95HsvCWCqcSWklIAdAyeLU0Nozm\nyYU12aA0eyHi5/LSR+xbbS4h/By95aR+IMdf+3BntGFR8qx9ppP5ZwCJxt9o/lU2\nY2Z5pOpqJ6L6zr1q8l82gyDDq4WDtYbNa7fyqCFoDEcOIzB8ML0YDE92ZhdSX5/l\nxYU4syB7jV3BN0LhkdBQ10qKG5dqEl+MoW/bWkZHMDizzqazVE0+ZR1aQMnpAfCq\nJh42aOTE9jmhJe1jFNmMDny0A+Ln1GlSAgNnGf4vuXVebwNzL/rNwepWAY4iFNRe\n0u8p8/AyAVAfnn0BVL4ep/yRheehGOP28++D/MwJWirKT+9ibakIetzCp9Ahtowt\nhBmaPY+QpXCdI1o2FXjI7a3jypgH8tFCHue9vwTXT0gTLL8vb2ynz4af8A9tLfm7\nxfkORIzsAjbRVPaNoCjy\n=rDx6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T17:06:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746","node_id":"C_kwDOPw6uhdoAKDAzNDQzN2UzNjU4YmQ0NjQ5Yzc1MmNjMTQ0MjdlNGU2ODk5M2E3NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b","sha":"d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b"}],"sha":"034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/034437e3658bd4649c752cc14427e4e68993a746"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:03:01Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:03:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(code-mapping): the upload dialog dropped the CSV before sending it (#1729)\n\nThe Code Mapping upload could not accept any file: the server always\nanswered \"CSV file is required.\" regardless of which CSV was chosen.\n\nThe shared api instance declares ''Content-Type: application/json'' as a\ndefault. axios reads that header when deciding how to encode the body, and\nfor FormData it takes the JSON branch -- it stringifies the entries, and\nevery File collapses to {}. The request that left the browser was\n`{\"file\":{},\"source_vocabulary_id\":\"...\",\"provenance\":\"...\"}` with a JSON\ncontent type, so the file was never on the wire. Clearing the header for\nthis one request lets the browser set multipart/form-data with its own\nboundary.\n\nThe existing test mocked @/api/axios wholesale, so it asserted against a\nmock that never carried the instance default and passed regardless. Two\ntests now cover it: one asserts the per-request header is cleared, and one\ndrives real axios to show the body stays FormData with the File intact while\nthe same body under the json default is flattened to \"file\":{}.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d454b2fa4bef6a0e66068681e8f4519b35c2a261","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/d454b2fa4bef6a0e66068681e8f4519b35c2a261"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b","verification":{"payload":"tree d454b2fa4bef6a0e66068681e8f4519b35c2a261\nparent b9a910c522379fdde1160f43325453d3c3094b33\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1791208981 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791208981 +0300\n\nfix(code-mapping): the upload dialog dropped the CSV before sending it (#1729)\n\nThe Code Mapping upload could not accept any file: the server always\nanswered \"CSV file is required.\" regardless of which CSV was chosen.\n\nThe shared api instance declares ''Content-Type: application/json'' as a\ndefault. axios reads that header when deciding how to encode the body, and\nfor FormData it takes the JSON branch -- it stringifies the entries, and\nevery File collapses to {}. The request that left the browser was\n`{\"file\":{},\"source_vocabulary_id\":\"...\",\"provenance\":\"...\"}` with a JSON\ncontent type, so the file was never on the wire. Clearing the header for\nthis one request lets the browser set multipart/form-data with its own\nboundary.\n\nThe existing test mocked @/api/axios wholesale, so it asserted against a\nmock that never carried the instance default and passed regardless. Two\ntests now cover it: one asserts the per-request header is cleared, and one\ndrives real axios to show the body stays FormData with the File intact while\nthe same body under the json default is flattened to \"file\":{}.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw64VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH2oQAA34SPfv/89dyPc66Xx7xtKR\nHh6wq48RIKHarAePmL+9xbUIKE2MpAVJX+lJ28Dys13V1Xn4C17CCHIfRfcVtdP0\natoNdWd+5CjC/deVoh