ithub.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/b9a910c522379fdde1160f43325453d3c3094b33"}],"sha":"d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/d69b19934d99f2fbf86a008ada23ed6c54134c2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adamblum","id":23161,"login":"adamblum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTYx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/b9a910c522379fdde1160f43325453d3c3094b33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:14:02Z","email":"adam@healthkey.ai","name":"Adam Blum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:14:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Record the approver and the suggest engine version as field mapping provenance (#1722)\n\n* Record the approver and the suggest engine version as field mapping provenance (#1719)\n\nFieldConceptMapping.provenance held only system_generated/curator, and\napproval deliberately left it alone, so an approved suggestion still read\nsystem_generated. Match Code Mapping (#1708):\n\n- provenance is free text (100 chars);\n- approving, or changing an approved recipe, stamps the approver;\n  an unapproved recipe edit is \"curator\"; un-approving keeps the name;\n- machine writers stamp a versioned engine: field-suggest v1 (reviewed |\n  lexical | propose-all), genomics-catalog v<version>;\n- migration 0279 names the reviewer on approved rows that have one.\n\nThe field mapper shows the stored text; legacy labels keep their names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: keep approver identity in this database (#1719)\n\n- An approver''s email never leaves: the inventory export and the curation\n  transfer carry it as \"curator\" (portable_provenance), as they already\n  clear reviewer. The transfer does the same for Code Mapping''s approver\n  stamp in origin_system (#1708), which had the same leak.\n- Changing an approved recipe signs off reviewer and reviewed_at with\n  provenance, so the three agree; only an approver signs off, anyone\n  else''s edit is \"curator\".\n- Migration 0279 stamps only system_generated and blank rows: a curator\n  row''s later edit may not be the reviewer''s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: drop every approver label in transfer; reversible 0279\n\n- Code Mapping approval stamps the email, else issuer|sub (or a name).\n  The transfer now drops origin_system matching any identity''s label on\n  the source instance, not only values containing \"@\".\n- Migration 0279''s reverse folds provenance back into\n  system_generated/curator before the column narrows to varchar(20).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Sign off reviewer with provenance on approved recipe edits (#1719)\n\nThe serializer half of the earlier review fix, left out of that commit:\nchanging an approved recipe sets reviewer, reviewed_at and provenance\ntogether, and only for a user who may approve; anyone else''s edit is\n\"curator\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"05e8d5e4bd6966ce2c4d98dd3fc571cdabb48689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/05e8d5e4bd6966ce2c4d98dd3fc571cdabb48689"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/b9a910c522379fdde1160f43325453d3c3094b33","verification":{"payload":"tree 05e8d5e4bd6966ce2c4d98dd3fc571cdabb48689\nparent 008c98565f3ea246ac90d8021d4529adcf5cdc40\nauthor Adam Blum <adam@healthkey.ai> 1791180842 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791180842 +0100\n\nRecord the approver and the suggest engine version as field mapping provenance (#1722)\n\n* Record the approver and the suggest engine version as field mapping provenance (#1719)\n\nFieldConceptMapping.provenance held only system_generated/curator, and\napproval deliberately left it alone, so an approved suggestion still read\nsystem_generated. Match Code Mapping (#1708):\n\n- provenance is free text (100 chars);\n- approving, or changing an approved recipe, stamps the approver;\n  an unapproved recipe edit is \"curator\"; un-approving keeps the name;\n- machine writers stamp a versioned engine: field-suggest v1 (reviewed |\n  lexical | propose-all), genomics-catalog v<version>;\n- migration 0279 names the reviewer on approved rows that have one.\n\nThe field mapper shows the stored text; legacy labels keep their names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: keep approver identity in this database (#1719)\n\n- An approver''s email never leaves: the inventory export and the curation\n  transfer carry it as \"curator\" (portable_provenance), as they already\n  clear reviewer. The transfer does the same for Code Mapping''s approver\n  stamp in origin_system (#1708), which had the same leak.\n- Changing an approved recipe signs off reviewer and reviewed_at with\n  provenance, so the three agree; only an approver signs off, anyone\n  else''s edit is \"curator\".\n- Migration 0279 stamps only system_generated and blank rows: a curator\n  row''s later edit may not be the reviewer''s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address review: drop every approver label in transfer; reversible 0279\n\n- Code Mapping approval stamps the email, else issuer|sub (or a name).\n  The transfer now drops origin_system matching any identity''s label on\n  the source instance, not only values containing \"@\".\n- Migration 0279''s reverse folds provenance back into\n  system_generated/curator before the column narrows to varchar(20).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Sign off reviewer with provenance on approved recipe edits (#1719)\n\nThe serializer half of the earlier review fix, left out of that commit:\nchanging an approved recipe sets reviewer, reviewed_at and provenance\ntogether, and only for a user who may approve; anyone else''s edit is\n\"curator\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw0AqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASSgQAI59j8+ctkUZUKQO0cu11h+6\nuO3ZBwJJUZO17rhMZLw4SsYuRdXVQxDDtA2dE2SCrIIt1NxpJdmphv9nTJXjEOHw\nE2gPbaPWylBpYEBVzx/amUXL9FHu0ddbY3PTsHx+B+nD29FP12S/qz1IE8iO3xho\nF0gBU8m3KtsVcQ/uHuQO4T/lo8yC44rPKKIQLYutBCyvSt1v2m2vb4KU9GVI4ykH\nmnRarVXiMZ+QBe9QUpVXXq7qoQPjmJlWSV6XzoeOkPz0aDJBbtdYy71EF3zYrD1l\nh5y9bUlhKLY+EyNOEE0ONnlo5sK5I7Q06PvppCCj/2yCoRwEYxCOiC6ZqXEx2FPW\nc5jJhGLRA8094v7m5L+gGhrqQ9TBdAKcrfQeb/mjAHKx/S0QbxLR1adTsnnj1jP6\nhSKl3WeLbZPOTyLuBnx44JwnPLLteXOCH5IlNB/hkr8ZJQw0CUoOPgxbZXrk1c2b\nR/5vfLYrixq1pSCu2bmqQbqe8laiDY0wBo3BmPS5J2nxSJa1YlIhA1L0tARG0q6I\nQl5Xfj00HbThMQPJ8ENkeDUd8cRwAIYZtfSkMuoTFNFPPIT79uk5VsQegobEmYQ3\n8biqDioEZx/Nbhl+PQIDt4hR9vtaEZk6M0v8NumBCCr5ltFlBFraZRMEzyYK78v7\ngmbBOl3YKDwLvRfzvdFR\n=uI9/\n-----END PGP S