bscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/adef176e8597aa48edf3a27aca6d447e5b49a5e6","node_id":"C_kwDOPw6uhdoAKGFkZWYxNzZlODU5N2FhNDhlZGYzYTI3YWNhNmQ0NDdlNWI0OWE1ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/031bbff774ef09d9b86b18587a162d7aabc788ab","sha":"031bbff774ef09d9b86b18587a162d7aabc788ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/031bbff774ef09d9b86b18587a162d7aabc788ab"}],"sha":"adef176e8597aa48edf3a27aca6d447e5b49a5e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/adef176e8597aa48edf3a27aca6d447e5b49a5e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/031bbff774ef09d9b86b18587a162d7aabc788ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:50:31Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:50:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(patient-detail): editor state no longer crosses patients or refreshes (#1668) (#1672)\n\n* fix(patient-detail): editor state no longer crosses patients or refreshes (#1668)\n\nPatientDetail builds every edit on pendingDataRef, the synchronous copy of\nthe editor state, and each save PATCHes what differs from the baseline.\nThat copy went stale in two ways:\n\n- Across patients: /patient/:personId rendered PatientDetail without a key,\n  so React Router kept one instance mounted when only the param changed.\n  B''s first edit was built on A''s values and PATCHed into B. The route now\n  renders PatientDetailRoute, which keys PatientDetail by personId, so\n  every ref, timer and piece of state resets per patient. PatientHome keys\n  its fixed-id instance the same way.\n\n- On the same patient: reloadPatientInfo, onRecordRefreshed and onConfirm\n  replaced editedInfo but not pendingDataRef, and two of them did not move\n  the baseline either, so the next edit sent pre-refresh values back.\n  All three now go through adoptServerRecord, which sets the baseline and\n  rebases edits still waiting for autosave onto the fresh record.\n\nThe new tests fail on dev: B''s PATCH carried {\"city\": \"Rome\",\n\"person_id\": 101}, and a post-refresh edit carried the stale derived\ncolumn.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(patient-detail): diff the save snapshot against the baseline read with it (#1668)\n\ndoSave took its snapshot of pendingDataRef before awaiting the\nwritable-field descriptor and read the baseline after it. A server\nrefresh landing in that window moves the baseline and rebases\npendingDataRef, so the old snapshot sent the server''s moved values back\nas edits. Both are now read together after the await.\n\nThe new test fails on the previous commit: the PATCH carried\n{\"city\": \"Rome\"} over the server''s \"Paris\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"27d891f05db27c131e0c8b8d6f82850fa3d3e197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/27d891f05db27c131e0c8b8d6f82850fa3d3e197"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/031bbff774ef09d9b86b18587a162d7aabc788ab","verification":{"payload":"tree 27d891f05db27c131e0c8b8d6f82850fa3d3e197\nparent f611e6dbf2bd1a4e4e7df70af07578994cf5c02a\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1790844631 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790844631 -0400\n\nfix(patient-detail): editor state no longer crosses patients or refreshes (#1668) (#1672)\n\n* fix(patient-detail): editor state no longer crosses patients or refreshes (#1668)\n\nPatientDetail builds every edit on pendingDataRef, the synchronous copy of\nthe editor state, and each save PATCHes what differs from the baseline.\nThat copy went stale in two ways:\n\n- Across patients: /patient/:personId rendered PatientDetail without a key,\n  so React Router kept one instance mounted when only the param changed.\n  B''s first edit was built on A''s values and PATCHed into B. The route now\n  renders PatientDetailRoute, which keys PatientDetail by personId, so\n  every ref, timer and piece of state resets per patient. PatientHome keys\n  its fixed-id instance the same way.\n\n- On the same patient: reloadPatientInfo, onRecordRefreshed and onConfirm\n  replaced editedInfo but not pendingDataRef, and two of them did not move\n  the baseline either, so the next edit sent pre-refresh values back.\n  All three now go through adoptServerRecord, which sets the baseline and\n  rebases edits still waiting for autosave onto the fresh record.\n\nThe new tests fail on dev: B''s PATCH carried {\"city\": \"Rome\",\n\"person_id\": 101}, and a post-refresh edit carried the stale derived\ncolumn.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(patient-detail): diff the save snapshot against the baseline read with it (#1668)\n\ndoSave took its snapshot of pendingDataRef before awaiting the\nwritable-field descriptor and read the baseline after it. A server\nrefresh landing in that window moves the baseline and rebases\npendingDataRef, so the old snapshot sent the server''s moved values back\nas edits. Both are now read together after the await.\n\nThe new test fails on the previous commit: the PATCH carried\n{\"city\": \"Rome\"} over the server''s \"Paris\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvh7XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhy0QAGHBJjpCgqCSwzuugiasgqh/\nMXo8SXwJLNDbnjzzulR74UWc0JclomVLf981IemlGc3PCPghb4B4mO57YsI2UR3s\nqSR0ZaQHqM9OA5/QsIzutTjloCytWzjIY+N2aRvqxVnZwl58KjrPwy5pFHFE2TGn\nSOhbqnh/0YSqnbK6MlFpGmS7E6ss601GZbhilnBJF+AwXy1/icXCKJCkQfSZjHJD\nDRkgxLC2A6qObtpIBYe+4x5+gPb+qbCexclePy1g1VuAwQqzcuUxGr3fg13bXKTX\n7WqJpTXie10tEnld53WsSKZKi2V2ENu6jTMTFOzixpeK9QYriZiASkWKqo4ke+Fo\nit2HxiQrgWJbikg3+0nrAecv8zQgN4ctwvn7gTGX7eNTJ2FVueKUOP6uyRd6qS9/\nmslL2C+ps6H3rJL+o2H7QbjSQxqDQRJWNicIJhDstv9pumTtTbvhvs4PUnf+X7Ee\n4UvsaMWXdpOKD7ZkuUU8b/lzNgVULZvaSyCzgXYl2t29KFg94s65ff4BD+eePRoo\nIDjUHY4OLIF96Mqx6ERRaeFuVcx3vwWNOF/7p7IEMqFaraB9M6mOgHMTy0iShLF4\nOm/dyA3Uekb16Mt8cGjVNxIMy5uWdAKacO0tmOtQ3UCeHp6Ajj5QuFMuaqxLx9CG\n0idERoWTBZ7N0FjSRTsl\n=Moyh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T08:50:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://