mmit/935d218f2cfa45e23af37cc1ab48d317ad61cbc6","sha":"935d218f2cfa45e23af37cc1ab48d317ad61cbc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/935d218f2cfa45e23af37cc1ab48d317ad61cbc6"}],"sha":"fac4d215e5bc936e16bee85311c9d5f4054623a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/fac4d215e5bc936e16bee85311c9d5f4054623a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/935d218f2cfa45e23af37cc1ab48d317ad61cbc6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:13:56Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:13:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Code Mapping: CancerBot vocabularies as a guarded catalog source (#1649) (#1653)\n\n* feat(code-mapping): CancerBot vocabularies as a guarded mapping source (#1649)\n\nRegister CB as a catalog source vocabulary: approving a CB row must not\nre-point clinical rows or mirror into concept_relationship, since no stored\nrow carries CB codes and the sweep would match other producers'' rows by label.\n\nAdd import_cb_vocabularies (seed proposed rows plus every named destination\nas candidates), approve_cb_mappings (bulk sign-off for auto_exact and curated,\nstamped with the reviewer) and export_cb_mappings (complete snapshot keyed by\nvocabulary_id + concept_code). Dry run by default.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(code-mapping): accept valid non-standard destinations for CB terms (#1649)\n\nCB''s committed therapy crosswalk uses HemOnc component concepts that are\nnon-standard in CTOMOP, and HK-* destinations are accepted by decision. A\nstandard-only rule kept 25 auto_exact and 5 curated proposals out of bulk\napproval. Refuse only absent, retired/replaced and mislabelled local ids.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(code-mapping): address review of the CB mapping source (#1649)\n\n- approve_cb_mappings: the destination check is part of the UPDATE, active\n  edit locks are honoured, the reviewer must be staff or org admin, and only\n  standard/classification, HK-* and HemOnc destinations are bulk-approved.\n- import_cb_vocabularies: require every column; re-resolve candidates and fill\n  a destination once its concept arrives, on rows nobody has edited; keep an\n  edited row''s description; dry run reports the same counts.\n- Candidates of catalog sources are selectable by the import rule, so the UI\n  offers what the importer accepts.\n- Drop the concept_relationship guard: CB rows never get a source concept.\n- CB tab no longer sorts first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(code-mapping): a re-import never sets destinations on CB rows (#1649)\n\nFilling a destination on re-import keyed on updated_by being null, but the\nUI''s clear path leaves it null, so a cleared proposal came back and could then\nbe bulk-approved. After the first import a row belongs to the reviewer: a\nre-run refreshes trial counts and candidates only, only on rows that still\ncarry the importer''s provenance, and lists rows whose proposal became usable.\nBulk approval uses the UI''s lock rule and names rows with no destination.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(code-mapping): a deleted CB row is re-proposed; reject it instead (#1649)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6cd4bfc1466efa5914e348809659f01d73c75d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/6cd4bfc1466efa5914e348809659f01d73c75d7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/935d218f2cfa45e23af37cc1ab48d317ad61cbc6","verification":{"payload":"tree 6cd4bfc1466efa5914e348809659f01d73c75d7d\nparent 8317acfa9ff3bcc4b28c6bf3da211dd2f1a99a13\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1790702036 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790702036 +0300\n\nCode Mapping: CancerBot vocabularies as a guarded catalog source (#1649) (#1653)\n\n* feat(code-mapping): CancerBot vocabularies as a guarded mapping source (#1649)\n\nRegister CB as a catalog source vocabulary: approving a CB row must not\nre-point clinical rows or mirror into concept_relationship, since no stored\nrow carries CB codes and the sweep would match other producers'' rows by label.\n\nAdd import_cb_vocabularies (seed proposed rows plus every named destination\nas candidates), approve_cb_mappings (bulk sign-off for auto_exact and curated,\nstamped with the reviewer) and export_cb_mappings (complete snapshot keyed by\nvocabulary_id + concept_code). Dry run by default.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(code-mapping): accept valid non-standard destinations for CB terms (#1649)\n\nCB''s committed therapy crosswalk uses HemOnc component concepts that are\nnon-standard in CTOMOP, and HK-* destinations are accepted by decision. A\nstandard-only rule kept 25 auto_exact and 5 curated proposals out of bulk\napproval. Refuse only absent, retired/replaced and mislabelled local ids.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(code-mapping): address review of the CB mapping source (#1649)\n\n- approve_cb_mappings: the destination check is part of the UPDATE, active\n  edit locks are honoured, the reviewer must be staff or org admin, and only\n  standard/classification, HK-* and HemOnc destinations are bulk-approved.\n- import_cb_vocabularies: require every column; re-resolve candidates and fill\n  a destination once its concept arrives, on rows nobody has edited; keep an\n  edited row''s description; dry run reports the same counts.\n- Candidates of catalog sources are selectable by the import rule, so the UI\n  offers what the importer accepts.\n- Drop the concept_relationship guard: CB rows never get a source concept.\n- CB tab no longer sorts first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(code-mapping): a re-import never sets destinations on CB rows (#1649)\n\nFilling a destination on re-import keyed on updated_by being null, but the\nUI''s clear path leaves it null, so a cleared proposal came back and could then\nbe bulk-approved. After the first import a row belongs to the reviewer: a\nre-run refreshes trial counts and candidates only, only on rows that still\ncarry the importer''s provenance, and lists rows whose proposal became usable.\nBulk approval uses the UI''s lock rule and names rows with no destination.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(code-mapping): a deleted CB row is re-proposed; reject it instead (#1649)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu/HUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUk0QAJGdgStu2sl90smwoI54QQrw\nQUVFxAydMZxnrFZGu/VpxorpG1FsKfptAhpXRLi/KLm