"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/9bf1d9574186e9f1239e37ba9871659a68b314c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:15:09Z","email":"adam@healthkey.ai","name":"Adam Blum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:15:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix athena-family origin matching and seenOnly default (#1648)\n\n* Fix athena-family origin_system matching and seenOnly default\n\nAthena-originated rows use various origin_system values beyond just\n''athena'' (e.g. athena-local-maps-to, athena-multiple, athena-standard-self).\nUse startswith(''athena'') / __startswith=''athena'' throughout browse and\nguard code so all athena-family rows land in the Athena Mapped section.\n\nAlso change the seenOnly toggle default to false so curators see all\ncodes by default, not just those with occurrence_count > 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply seen_only filter to Unmapped section only\n\nThe Seen > 0 toggle now narrows only the Unmapped section. Mapped,\nRejected and Athena Mapped show all codes regardless of occurrence_count,\nso curators see the full reference set while focusing the work queue on\ncodes patients actually have.\n\nBackend: browse_mappings no longer applies seen_only to the global\nqueryset. Instead it filters the Unmapped section query and count after\nsection carving. The search/provenance aggregate path adds the\noccurrence_count condition only to the unmapped bucket. visible_rows\naccepts an optional section parameter so the group-members endpoint\napplies the same per-section logic.\n\nFrontend: seenOnly defaults back to true — the checkbox starts checked\nand the API sends seen_only=1 on initial load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Exclude athena-multiple from resolved Athena origins\n\nathena-multiple means Athena found several candidates and a curator has\nnot chosen yet — it belongs in Unmapped, not Athena Mapped. Only resolved\norigins (athena, athena-local-maps-to, athena-standard-self) land in the\nAthena Mapped section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Adam Blum <adam@dplrn.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2c56271f89952809c56c7e2693000bd982373ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/e2c56271f89952809c56c7e2693000bd982373ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/9bf1d9574186e9f1239e37ba9871659a68b314c2","verification":{"payload":"tree e2c56271f89952809c56c7e2693000bd982373ec\nparent 8798ec244376e973e6c3a2a09a777679db6e92d7\nauthor Adam Blum <adam@healthkey.ai> 1790698509 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790698509 -0400\n\nFix athena-family origin matching and seenOnly default (#1648)\n\n* Fix athena-family origin_system matching and seenOnly default\n\nAthena-originated rows use various origin_system values beyond just\n''athena'' (e.g. athena-local-maps-to, athena-multiple, athena-standard-self).\nUse startswith(''athena'') / __startswith=''athena'' throughout browse and\nguard code so all athena-family rows land in the Athena Mapped section.\n\nAlso change the seenOnly toggle default to false so curators see all\ncodes by default, not just those with occurrence_count > 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Apply seen_only filter to Unmapped section only\n\nThe Seen > 0 toggle now narrows only the Unmapped section. Mapped,\nRejected and Athena Mapped show all codes regardless of occurrence_count,\nso curators see the full reference set while focusing the work queue on\ncodes patients actually have.\n\nBackend: browse_mappings no longer applies seen_only to the global\nqueryset. Instead it filters the Unmapped section query and count after\nsection carving. The search/provenance aggregate path adds the\noccurrence_count condition only to the unmapped bucket. visible_rows\naccepts an optional section parameter so the group-members endpoint\napplies the same per-section logic.\n\nFrontend: seenOnly defaults back to true — the checkbox starts checked\nand the API sends seen_only=1 on initial load.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Exclude athena-multiple from resolved Athena origins\n\nathena-multiple means Athena found several candidates and a curator has\nnot chosen yet — it belongs in Unmapped, not Athena Mapped. Only resolved\norigins (athena, athena-local-maps-to, athena-standard-self) land in the\nAthena Mapped section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Adam Blum <adam@dplrn.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+QNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+ggQADWPIgR88iwzj1+fF/WModsL\npy8YkehFzwAlPJwQA/VZqC7IxHf6blghJsxPmHzj8bNMviHT3qKr83iHzWZ/o9Nf\nmQxqzFVjXTuH4vfFk+VAERkIzPWOA6iatBJSzNq0RgUE263n3wlyNVMqVdnxxdei\nL9vwmLcfFIWSKJfGQbB7T6OvQDn24RjMHBPVON3dNH1lt07TNF1HvsNbv8gJyQl9\nYbSGtG+qp1jlBmjWC6/xEy+qJXknO2nA2+VCvmk7y6dhfUlBdm1d5cPiGzkwWxC4\nfXwj5VFP7+VSNl5kgzgOXh9hcu1+eR5P6/Cb2lHEnedM0W8mezicOhFud8Nw1L6L\nr2kei1opfgLwbPv65AHFwITgx3dGbc9ii5eduahvq5AtyWl914tzQfGomD5LX6b9\n2wDScSVJAiAPWnScpJAdoLIQP5cPBUFpnfRqyCp8VMzkpDgPpj8GIwWgiyM1r38F\nxHPeJ1z5+CrWqeGpt33XzXIczhZK3/+lg8eqNdXiYChY3O3DMhNLSMGsOWUYfiU9\nBNwSp/6A8Y9c4lJGxHJDoylLJBf9HNEG6jyIx6WkBLGFdTJj2Hea5hDf7hmfiJww\ntJMEl3AxwJJQ+pwjMsXXtwfwdLJ2O/fK4qpDI4Hf8KKdM4qfyURxU1zga7PsChA9\ncCEKKI6TMFNmN54g11cr\n=65+s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T16:15:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/9bf1d9574186e9f1239e37ba9871659a68b314c2","node_id":"C_kwDOPw6uhdoAKDliZjFkOTU3NDE4NmU5ZjEyMzllMzdiYTk4NzE2NTlhNjhiMzE0YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/promop/commit/8798ec244376e973e6c3a2a09a777679db6e92d7","sha":"8798ec244376e973e6c3a2a09a777679db6e92d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/8798ec244376e973e6c3a2a09a777679db6e92d7"}],"sha":"9bf1d9574186e9f1239e37ba9871659a68b314c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/9bf1d9574186e9f1239e37ba9871659a68b314c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23161?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adamblum","id":23161,"login":"adamblum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTYx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamblum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/8798ec244376e973e6c3a2a09a777679db6e92d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:31:39Z","email":"adam@healthkey.ai","name":"Adam Blum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:31:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Relabel ICD10 to ICD10CM in SCCM (#1643)\n\n* Relabel ICD10 to ICD10CM and remove cross-vocab machinery\n\nNo ICD-10 (WHO) vocabulary is loaded -- only ICD10CM. All 12,994 SCCM rows\nwith source_vocabulary_id=ICD10 are ICD-10-CM codes. After the tab split\n(#1632), these were stranded on an ICD-10 tab for a vocabulary that does not\nexist, while the ICD-10-CM tab showed only the 9,316 Athena rows.\n\nMigration 0266 relabels ICD10 to ICD10CM (single UPDATE, idempotent).\nRemoves ICD10_CROSS_VOCAB, ICD10_CANONICAL, ICD10CM_MERGE, and all\ncross-vocabulary hint machinery that bridged the two. Adds HemOnc,\nRxNorm Extension, ATC, CVX to SOURCE_TAB_ORDER so all mappings are\nvisible on a tab.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix code review findings: update tests, commands, and guards for ICD10CM\n\n- Reverse migration is now a documented no-op (original split unrecoverable)\n- athena_mapping_guard restores ICD10CM-specific None-destination fast path\n- FHIR_ALIASES in import_healthtree_seen_counts maps WHO ICD-10 URIs to ICD10CM\n- reconcile_athena_mappings and scrape_unmapped_destinations default to ICD10CM\n- All test files updated to reflect post-migration reality (ICD10CM only)\n- Removed obsolete cross-vocab alias tests; rewrote enrichment tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix CI: renumber migration to 0267 and update remaining test files\n\n- Renumber migration 0266→0267 (0266_loincrelease landed on dev first)\n- test_import_healthtree_seen_counts: default vocab ICD10→ICD10CM, fix\n  all CSV vocabs and assertions for post-migration reality\n- test_backfill_source_descriptions: ICD10→ICD10CM for source descriptions\n- test_athena_mapping_reconciliation: remove ICD10 alias cases, both\n  HT-One and curator ICD10CM rows are now reconciled\n- test_athena_destinations: use generic CUSTOM_ICD for --lookup-vocabulary\n  feature test (no ICD10 rows exist after migration)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: restore SOURCE_TAB_ORDER to match dev (remove unintended additions)\n\nHemOnc, ATC, CVX, and RxNorm Extension were accidentally added to\nSOURCE_TAB_ORDER during the ICD10 cleanup. These low-volume vocabularies\nshould not be in the static tab order — they appear dynamically only when\nthey have proposals.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Adam Blum <adam@dplrn.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53407d672b2ad458bebbb5edb1b897a498a4e722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/53407d672b2ad458bebbb5edb1b897a498a4e722"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/8798ec244376e973e6c3a2a09a777679db6e92d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 53407d672b2ad458bebbb5edb1b897a498a4e722\nparent a4d4f0bb6e414e2a7e948b85f3ec3546d142d6c2\nauthor Adam Blum <adam@healthkey.ai> 1790692299 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790692299 +0100\n\nRelabel ICD10 to ICD10CM in SCCM (#1643)\n\n* Relabel ICD10 to ICD10CM and remove cross-vocab machinery\n\nNo ICD-10 (WHO) vocabulary is loaded -- only ICD10CM. All 12,994 SCCM rows\nwith source_vocabulary_id=ICD10 are ICD-10-CM codes. After the tab split\n(#1632), these were stranded on an ICD-10 tab for a vocabulary that does not\nexist, while the ICD-10-CM tab showed only the 9,316 Athena rows.\n\nMigration 0266 relabels ICD10 to ICD10CM (single UPDATE, idempotent).\nRemoves ICD10_CROSS_VOCAB, ICD10_CANONICAL, ICD10CM_MERGE, and all\ncross-vocabulary hint machinery that bridged the two. Adds HemOnc,\nRxNorm Extension, ATC, CVX to SOURCE_TAB_ORDER so all mappings are\nvisible on a tab.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix code review findings: update tests, commands, and guards for ICD10CM\n\n- Reverse migration is now a documented no-op (original split unrecoverable)\n- athena_mapping_guard restores ICD10CM-specific None-destination fast path\n- FHIR_ALIASES in import_healthtree_seen_counts maps WHO ICD-10 URIs to ICD10CM\n- reconcile_athena_mappings and scrape_unmapped_destinations default to ICD10CM\n- All test files updated to reflect post-migration reality (ICD10CM only)\n- Removed obsolete cross-vocab alias tests; rewrote enrichment tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix CI: renumber migration to 0267 and update remaining test files\n\n- Renumber migration 0266→0267 (0266_loincrelease landed on dev first)\n- test_import_healthtree_seen_counts: default vocab ICD10→ICD10CM, fix\n  all CSV vocabs and assertions for post-migration reality\n- test_backfill_source_descriptions: ICD10→ICD10CM for source descriptions\n- test_athena_mapping_reconciliation: remove ICD10 alias cases, both\n  HT-One and curator ICD10CM rows are now reconciled\n- test_athena_destinations: use generic CUSTOM_ICD for --lookup-vocabulary\n  feature test (no ICD10 rows exist after migration)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: restore SOURCE_TAB_ORDER to match dev (remove unintended additions)\n\nHemOnc, ATC, CVX, and RxNorm Extension were accidentally added to\nSOURCE_TAB_ORDER during the ICD10 cleanup. These low-volume vocabularies\nshould not be in the static tab order — they appear dynamically only when\nthey have proposals.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Adam Blum <adam@dplrn.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu8vLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6oAQABuG6rHGC6UJe1LIloMaKuPC\n6KbT9AXx6s2XGlU+eQruGQr2Dv5Le+chg31EsARd+qmzreJ0J2eYyPLPJ9G5WA6S\npi3t0fWNnIz/mSdTDfl/Fng/wOOKa9Ndxj1on3ze2CcCxtTzvIUFCK6p1M5g2avb\nFxBANxflz4DGPZ6JeY1pFHXmem+OomWnF7g4aHK60YJQvbb7Jug5rBx2jQ+bRTa3\n++F/lZldmxje7CY/MBKFzQA5VEmVoECJhy9vk5Vv1u9DTF8f7k5RKXPnDNTcB7rk\nNliZ5NbhWclRB/cqLvPsWxi85wsCiXZ4tJxJ1XZD0IKSQdBCHOA2uQTEIQ/0vDZZ\ndkZn6pf2PMcrQh2AGaLNxK0zcfVOs/evlEkT391WA0FCghECrVTG807L5OsWGx6Y\nvRyWkRL0Dg1d6OHctNNXBLumnSu+OZ5LJZX5etLynRA849ICmdzUhKJik5IR3VCb\n5WXCV7Jwq+dDpoU/gBAMXB2OuGS/zcjv2DzqpDSiBmn6QeX1Y93KECYVDyuZOBwB\nhJsHeg99FeyuhocC9Fp4qwRqUrut4BM20VyI55556k8j2lkJEvZ2z0WJME7QTvE9\nqwSU+XgLifVsjlDxg+ypifS+Oq+99F/bg0LQqnYXQ9cqv+S/6bIzhG2TWgFr583c\nmOSMDrw8tpUZhz3d5qAp\n=I6OU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T14:31:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_u