,"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsburgess/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/larsburgess","id":23724,"login":"larsburgess","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNzI0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsburgess/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsburgess/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsburgess/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsburgess/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsburgess/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsburgess","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/commits/a426a0f2b075e47972f0d18d5876bfda093654e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:33:44Z","email":"larsburgess@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lars Burgess"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:33:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"HKI-SEC-08: decide PHI encryption at rest and automate its evidence (#1564)\n\n* feat(security): decide PHI encryption at rest and automate its evidence (#60)\n\nPlatform-managed AES-256 with provider-held keys is the mechanism; no\napplication-level field encryption of clinical data. Recorded in\ndocs/soc2/encryption-at-rest.md.\n\nmanage.py capture_encryption_evidence derives the PHI stores from live\nsettings and, with --render, reads the backing Render resources. It\nemits no hostnames or credentials, fails on any API error, and\n--require-covered exits 1 on a gap. It already reports one: patient\ndocuments on the ephemeral filesystem (#1563). Scheduling is #1562.\n\nAdds SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS and a SECRET_KEY rotation procedure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): count unmatched Celery backends as gaps; read Render ids from the deployment\n\nA Celery broker or result backend that is not a Render Key Value is now a\ngap, even beside one that is. The --render-postgres-id and\n--render-service-id overrides are removed: ids come only from the live\nconnection URLs and Render''s RENDER_SERVICE_ID, so a capture can only\ndescribe the resources it runs against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): report remote file storage and a separate Redis cache\n\nOn a deployment, a file storage backend without a local path (S3 and the\nlike) is now a gap: the collector cannot inspect it, so it is not assumed\ncovered. The Django cache''s Redis location (CACHE_URL or the shared\nbroker) joins the deduplicated key-value inventory, since it holds\nthrottle counters and cached token lookups.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"caf5c16d7e166e77b7f0b71b444f40b451ed3e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/trees/caf5c16d7e166e77b7f0b71b444f40b451ed3e5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/promop/git/commits/a426a0f2b075e47972f0d18d5876bfda093654e1","verification":{"payload":"tree caf5c16d7e166e77b7f0b71b444f40b451ed3e5d\nparent 0be09758e52d21297c74a42b1908c2c3e2d5f461\nauthor Lars Burgess <larsburgess@users.noreply.github.com> 1790436824 -1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790436824 +0100\n\nHKI-SEC-08: decide PHI encryption at rest and automate its evidence (#1564)\n\n* feat(security): decide PHI encryption at rest and automate its evidence (#60)\n\nPlatform-managed AES-256 with provider-held keys is the mechanism; no\napplication-level field encryption of clinical data. Recorded in\ndocs/soc2/encryption-at-rest.md.\n\nmanage.py capture_encryption_evidence derives the PHI stores from live\nsettings and, with --render, reads the backing Render resources. It\nemits no hostnames or credentials, fails on any API error, and\n--require-covered exits 1 on a gap. It already reports one: patient\ndocuments on the ephemeral filesystem (#1563). Scheduling is #1562.\n\nAdds SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS and a SECRET_KEY rotation procedure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): count unmatched Celery backends as gaps; read Render ids from the deployment\n\nA Celery broker or result backend that is not a Render Key Value is now a\ngap, even beside one that is. The --render-postgres-id and\n--render-service-id overrides are removed: ids come only from the live\nconnection URLs and Render''s RENDER_SERVICE_ID, so a capture can only\ndescribe the resources it runs against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): report remote file storage and a separate Redis cache\n\nOn a deployment, a file storage backend without a local path (S3 and the\nlike) is now a gap: the collector cannot inspect it, so it is not assumed\ncovered. The Django cache''s Redis location (CACHE_URL or the shared\nbroker) joins the deduplicated key-value inventory, since it holds\nthrottle counters and cached token lookups.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+XYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAghIQAIpz10HYGCpC7kyItxz0Q4vn\nJJaJIVH7BG2+A27O1jQTJKpuPv3V2CzxQ07SKGplJwYxYJmtRxzPJPc++W1UyKtK\nZc0y79B/GzuRDtzwoPGJjf8YRtzReO2NU4buDMJWk7cRRMupqO8NuVmRs8CNmzn0\nnq9A7eHLMPO+l2PQUSJT4+cWiKwb2/vBVQZF/z6YHOCKcyt6DSBMF4r95efvhXnY\nab4VOy+BNAZZnE/gv5L2mN/BH4gXnvS882oOJiRGcb+FIgFWV/yq9/EwfL0xmUif\npc6kutg6ADJsFsfZveyHfEYsKrxVlVSocCTr7WQcHZgPdHkZbbU2oGHqIIcoXkDW\nia3rnLCmotNJK8MGslJEwODebkwgPPNsvMPjVdGBLG9pCjWntb2hisiEKU2jLpoO\no8Mfgu5lglibx8RmeP35Iu8GtGaZ/nEuydTj+SOxwQb/QD9oEz/8Oi97561DyzlB\nCEMfReDW0DNrwiZCPtKcrrYWxCkQYq/0t64U9PnajcpXENaBhvzCEgUQoKtAB73B\nJnXYASwTWEfU0JxA5DUVbuNvV2b1MOC7