epo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/commits/4035abd7aa3b45db5eeeb0de0f43019fb1aab6b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-03T01:56:41Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-03T01:56:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STHUB-20 supply eslint v10 config; lint source (#14)\n\nThis does not leverage eslint-config-stripes because it uses modern\nESLint, v10. I feel like our v7 rules are not really worth preserving in\nlight of the deprecation of formatting rules in v8, the widespread\nadoption of Prettier and (I think?) the realization that AirBnB''s\nformatting rules were less timelessly classic than just temporarily\ntrendy. Also it just felt dumb to double-down on an EOLed version.\n\nBut I acknowledge this is a rogue move and would 100% accept closing\nthis PR as \"dude, don''t rock the boat, yes v10 is great but let''s be\ndeliberate, not sneaky.\"\n\nRefs STHUB-20\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ryan Berger <rberger@ebsco.com>","tree":{"sha":"80e5dbde9f611a2b8a2c5e74d491817df97c5cc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/git/trees/80e5dbde9f611a2b8a2c5e74d491817df97c5cc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/git/commits/4035abd7aa3b45db5eeeb0de0f43019fb1aab6b4","verification":{"payload":"tree 80e5dbde9f611a2b8a2c5e74d491817df97c5cc0\nparent 268356f910b781e514fe4031b4649f2d028e0695\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1772503001 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772503001 -0500\n\nSTHUB-20 supply eslint v10 config; lint source (#14)\n\nThis does not leverage eslint-config-stripes because it uses modern\nESLint, v10. I feel like our v7 rules are not really worth preserving in\nlight of the deprecation of formatting rules in v8, the widespread\nadoption of Prettier and (I think?) the realization that AirBnB''s\nformatting rules were less timelessly classic than just temporarily\ntrendy. Also it just felt dumb to double-down on an EOLed version.\n\nBut I acknowledge this is a rogue move and would 100% accept closing\nthis PR as \"dude, don''t rock the boat, yes v10 is great but let''s be\ndeliberate, not sneaky.\"\n\nRefs STHUB-20\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ryan Berger <rberger@ebsco.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJppj/ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtgQQAGOXPawMNFBKb4LHTjJpE76o\nic9wM2a/S8KiMJpgylj6VsBCnsrEZyybBB3fTBOWkTLNDJMTDznGq0ILfXSZt8r3\nfJkq1cbyXvtappdfDSD6DCT7Nmdczgi8K8BooPws1auw4B7EnqzMjDspNN0dGAj8\nmUfwtDFmUROS0lKBWiv7kZVdahVfoSMWddZMv85QRmBj2k5LuvXt7EWc0CReZ2kh\nDLcbKVfT57YCauX4S6jL3g7ixRNhGy1hdA3FnEM3lpadJrBaew4UKS+gEiCVPL2i\nyrfoNvL7Qa1erzz19hytv9naBo9uNHKKaZT7lQbtQsxQqN4SB4cj1CRN7QaxoCas\n9Hm5CjM33WaPsbq+qXoqVYZok2dyW2He2AbO3g/BtKY82VrsYLCqM4731nWTekc4\nqrJ6EnoCYJmqJWk/prLsqPIw0W0Ae6NOHijjPQ7+72ZlCvoh96Y4S/GrhrWJPA1x\nm22herqyr8KcJ+Vba0AdWfVNu2l5QuMQwiDNn+nKQmp//P3Tup9m2NOzKPt1iL4g\nhrWGJaZ96sQx5Pp3yrUk1IQHeKQYX1MacEARs5M5tcFMIKGFmR4PNtYUP8mory+b\nJImtmYvj1aNwRlJAh34MPF+VdF45Mgb6CwTzEdNLZ3NTkkL0Unj1YB4WZMcsFbXH\n9AAY2+MkVO8Ny8bxWIGK\n=Bfkz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-03T01:56:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-hub/commit/4035abd7aa3b45db5eeeb0de0f43019fb1aab6b4","node_id":"C_kwDOPyoLndoAKDQwMzVhYmQ3YWEzYjQ1ZGI1ZWVlYjBkZTBmNDMwMTlmYjFhYWI2YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-hub/commit/268356f910b781e514fe4031b4649f2d028e0695","sha":"268356f910b781e514fe4031b4649f2d028e0695","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/commits/268356f910b781e514fe4031b4649f2d028e0695"}],"sha":"4035abd7aa3b45db5eeeb0de0f43019fb1aab6b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/commits/4035abd7aa3b45db5eeeb0de0f43019fb1aab6b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/commits/268356f910b781e514fe4031b4649f2d028e0695/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-27T22:07:20Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-27T22:07:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STHUB-11 💀 handle fatal startup errors (#13)\n\nAny error that occurs during entitlement or discovery API requests, or\nrelated to loading Stripes (the host application) is fatal: if Stripes\ncannot load, nothing can load. Trap these errors. Display something\nfriendly for the user in the browser. Log something helpful for the\ndeveloper in the console.\n\nThe user may be in a delicate state here: they have successfully\nauthenticated but have not successfully started a session. Thus, the\nerror page includes two buttons:\n1. reload: maybe the failure was the result of a temporary blip and\n   entitlement/discovery will run correctly\n2. logout: make an API request to `/logout` to destroy any cookies and\n   then redirect back to /, allowing login to begin again\n\nErrors are logged to the console in the catch clause where they are\nfirst trapped. If the fetch succeeds but the response-code is not ok,\ncall `await response.json()` there in the catch clause (there''s no harm;\nthat function is already async by definition) and include it in the\nerror that is thrown, simplifying parsing in the error page.\n\nRefs STHUB-11","tree":{"sha":"32e7085dc9fba30f14250d1eec42b1bfb346ead7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/git/trees/32e7085dc9fba30f14250d1eec42b1bfb346ead7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-hub/git/commits/268356f910b781e514fe4031b4649f2d028e0695","verification":{"payload":"tree 32e7085dc9fba30f14250d1eec42b1bfb346ead7\nparent 0bdbc0b19a82bd2a9ecf8f38d2242739c02dfa29\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1772230040 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772230040 -0500\n\nSTHUB-11 💀 handle fatal startup errors (#13)\n\nAny error that occurs during entitlement or discovery API requests, or\nrelated to loading Stripes (the host application) is fatal: if Stripes\ncannot load, nothing can load. Trap these errors. Display something\nfriendly for the user in the browser. Log something helpful for the\ndeveloper in the console.\n\nThe user may be in a delicate state here: they have successfully\nauthenticated but have not successfully started a session. Thus, the\nerror page includes two buttons:\n1. reload: maybe the failure was the result of a temporary blip and\n   entitlement/discovery will run correctly\n2. logout: make an API request to `/logout` to destroy any cookies and\n   then redirect back to /, allowing login to begin again\n\nErrors are logged to the console in the catch clause where they are\nfirst trapped. If the fetch succeeds but the response-code is not ok,\ncall `await response.json()` there in the catch clause (there''s no harm;\nthat function is already async by definition) and include it in the\nerror that is thrown, simplifying parsing in the error page.\n\nRefs STHUB-11","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpohWYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3XAQAFO8w4ESa5a1MObrq4w+iUKM\nk24we77ptkFSuKXGW/ASNFLfrP7IbLaN67R+aGObXMCngUdNcHoJR5QtaxlXO6Rq\nPnmt6ItwkoXcZf21FWkuFEL6QYEzgmlUeQe5qVLQsLfxD16yavGX0/JHP4jhm7+H\n6ppZej1Xtaz2w06xIgF+pmGoAds9frCZ7OSrX0FiwKdIWoISISH7yE+MupR2cJQb\nwEkHNfZcFbLOtuL7yHlgbvsGb1kYvA1pc/TQvxfWIRXW0X1M+yj2OCOkSTvoJOvg\n5XHDs+qwRCv7hCleKWKIHqpqWk1SpdCwcyZafMDDxGChRs3EZJdbjPGBQqKV76PL\n+lu0R9dTK02TiPtxcIcdG3HUDyZdgmq+NYxzLi5ccWVPyuLp59FrtQJ08pFxIJh4\nJbVmuzN+t7RZVfKBSrTa7/E6GoomhhiA7gfTy/51Jz746tbhbmD7xN4EtkOTSHI8\nBookoANEunuJD2+KRkOUuk1r0flnm/eyp8hyxXpiUa+bXGOQfxJ3/cSbtdNWXliP\nO/VibhdfF8vKMbkIE5/Zpxl82WI5Xsu9LUmHOhgXXh4hq2Z393Au05rGUmE9loPy\ngMZhSOsIur64E1c6kYGMuSiRCGsC3+aKdI/WcV8Az0lAKW/MFvmALT2We9AHvZMb\nTqy9FSdubExv6qPXkwNy\n=kllz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-27T22:07:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.githu